{"task_id": "healthcare_and_medicine/6111/global", "answer": "This is a concerning post-procedural presentation in an elderly patient with multiple risk factors. Let me analyze the differential diagnosis and recommended workup.\n\n## Clinical Assessment\n\nThis patient presents with **post-procedural fever with hemodynamic changes** (tachycardia, hypoxia, fever) occurring 1 hour after hysteroscopic D&C for pyometra. The timing and clinical picture are highly concerning for **sepsis**.\n\n---\n\n## Differential Diagnosis of Fever\n\n### Most Likely (High Priority)\n\n| Cause | Supporting Evidence |\n|-------|---------------------|\n| **Urosepsis/Procedure-related bacteremia** | Pyometra instrumentation can introduce bacteria into bloodstream; classic presentation with chills, fever, tachycardia within 1 hour |\n| **Worsening pneumonia** | Pre-existing bilateral pneumonia; SpO2 drop to 90% suggests respiratory compromise |\n| **Acute endometritis/pelvic infection** | Pyometra + D&C creates risk for ascending/spreading infection |\n\n### Important to Consider\n\n- **Aspiration pneumonia** — IV anesthesia in elderly patient with pre-existing respiratory infection\n- **Septic emboli** — From uterine veins to pulmonary circulation (could explain both respiratory and systemic symptoms)\n- **Fluid overload** — From uterine irrigation fluid absorption (less likely to cause high fever)\n\n### Less Likely\n\n- Drug fever (timing too acute)\n- Malignant hyperthermia (presentation doesn't match classic pattern)\n- Transfusion reaction (no mention of blood products)\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Laboratory Tests and Examinations\n\n### Immediate (Within 1 Hour)\n\n| Test | Rationale |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Blood cultures × 2 sets** (before antibiotics) | Identify causative organism; essential for sepsis workup |\n| **CBC with differential** | WBC count, left shift, hemoglobin (bleeding?), platelets (DIC screening) |\n| **Serum lactate** | Marker of tissue hypoperfusion; prognostic in sepsis |\n| **Arterial blood gas (ABG)** | Assess oxygenation, acid-base status |\n| **Procalcitonin** | Helps distinguish bacterial sepsis from other causes |\n| **Coagulation profile** (PT/PTT/INR, fibrinogen, D-dimer) | Screen for DIC in severe sepsis |\n\n### Microbiology\n\n| Test | Rationale |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Endometrial/cervical cultures** | From D&C specimens — identify uterine pathogens |\n| **Sputum culture** | Given pneumonia, identify respiratory pathogens |\n| **Urinalysis + urine culture** | Rule out concurrent UTI as sepsis source |\n\n### Imaging\n\n| Test | Rationale |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Repeat chest X-ray or CT** | Assess pneumonia progression, rule out aspiration, septic emboli |\n| **Transvaginal ultrasound** | Evaluate for retained products, uterine perforation, pelvic abscess |\n| **Pelvic CT (if unstable)** | Better visualization of pelvic infection/abscess |\n\n### Additional Labs\n\n| Test | Rationale |\n|------|-----------|\n| **Comprehensive metabolic panel** | Electrolytes, renal function, liver function |\n| **CRP** | Inflammatory marker (trend for response) |\n| **Type and screen** | In case transfusion needed |\n| **Troponin/BNP** | Elderly patient with sepsis — screen for cardiac involvement |\n\n---\n\n## Immediate Management Considerations\n\n1. **Sepsis protocol** — IV fluids, broad-spectrum antibiotics (consider expanding coverage beyond moxifloxacin to include anaerobes and gram-negatives given pyometra)\n2. **Oxygen supplementation** — SpO2 90% requires immediate support\n3. **Hemodynamic monitoring** — Consider ICU transfer given age and sepsis signs\n4. **Gynecology consultation** — Evaluate for need for additional drainage or surgical intervention\n\n---\n\n## Key Clinical Concern\n\nThe combination of **pyometra + instrumentation + rapid post-procedural fever with hemodynamic changes** is classic for **procedure-induced bacteremia/sepsis**. The uterine cavity in pyometra contains purulent material with high bacterial load; D&C can force bacteria into uterine veins and systemic circulation. This is a **medical emergency** requiring immediate sepsis management.\n\nWould you like me to elaborate on the antibiotic selection considerations or the specific diagnostic criteria for sepsis in this context?", "score": {"rubric_results": [{"rubric_number": 1, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型明确将脓毒症/菌血症列为首要诊断和高优先级原因，符合评分要求。"}, {"rubric_number": 2, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型未引用《2023 年中国宫腔积脓诊治专家共识》，也未明确说明诊刮不作为常规推荐。"}, {"rubric_number": 3, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型未明确提及患者符合 SIRS 标准，仅提及脓毒症，缺乏对体温和心率的具体标准判定。"}, {"rubric_number": 4, "weight": 4, "met": false, "reason": "模型未具体指出术前仅治疗 3 天且未复查 CT 这一细节及其对发热的影响。"}, {"rubric_number": 5, "weight": 3, "met": false, "reason": "模型鉴别诊断中未包含急性肺栓塞（PE），仅提及感染性栓子。"}, {"rubric_number": 6, "weight": 4, "met": true, "reason": "模型列出了子宫穿孔和盆腔感染等手术相关并发症作为潜在原因。"}, {"rubric_number": 7, "weight": 3, "met": false, "reason": "模型推荐了乳酸检测，但未提及 Sepsis-3 标准作为依据。"}, {"rubric_number": 8, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型未明确说明需采集需氧 + 厌氧、不同穿刺点或寒战时采血等细节。"}, {"rubric_number": 9, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型未引用专家共识，也未明确提及药敏试验。"}, {"rubric_number": 10, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型完整列出了 CBC、CRP 和 PCT 检测。"}, {"rubric_number": 11, "weight": 3, "met": false, "reason": "模型推荐了 D-二聚体，但目的是筛查 DIC 而非排除肺栓塞。"}, {"rubric_number": 12, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型明确建议复查胸片或 CT 以评估肺炎变化。"}, {"rubric_number": 13, "weight": 4, "met": true, "reason": "模型建议了盆腔超声或 CT 以评估穿孔及感染情况。"}, {"rubric_number": 14, "weight": 2, "met": true, "reason": "模型明确建议了尿常规和尿培养以排除其他感染源。"}, {"rubric_number": 15, "weight": -4, "met": false, "reason": "模型未引用参考文献，比例未超过 30%，不触发扣分。"}, {"rubric_number": 16, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "病理生理学内容比例适中，未造成冗余，不触发扣分。"}, {"rubric_number": 17, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "回复结构清晰，符合临床逻辑，未出现 verbose 或组织混乱，不触发扣分。"}, {"rubric_number": 18, "weight": -4, "met": false, "reason": "模型使用标准医学术语，未出现社会科学术语，不触发扣分。"}], "score": 21, "max_score": 56, "raw_response": "[\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确将脓毒症/菌血症列为首要诊断和高优先级原因，符合评分要求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 2,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未引用《2023 年中国宫腔积脓诊治专家共识》，也未明确说明诊刮不作为常规推荐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 3,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未明确提及患者符合 SIRS 标准，仅提及脓毒症，缺乏对体温和心率的具体标准判定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 4,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未具体指出术前仅治疗 3 天且未复查 CT 这一细节及其对发热的影响。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 5,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型鉴别诊断中未包含急性肺栓塞（PE），仅提及感染性栓子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 6,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型列出了子宫穿孔和盆腔感染等手术相关并发症作为潜在原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 7,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型推荐了乳酸检测，但未提及 Sepsis-3 标准作为依据。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 8,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未明确说明需采集需氧 + 厌氧、不同穿刺点或寒战时采血等细节。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 9,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未引用专家共识，也未明确提及药敏试验。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 10,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型完整列出了 CBC、CRP 和 PCT 检测。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 11,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型推荐了 D-二聚体，但目的是筛查 DIC 而非排除肺栓塞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 12,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确建议复查胸片或 CT 以评估肺炎变化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 13,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型建议了盆腔超声或 CT 以评估穿孔及感染情况。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 14,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确建议了尿常规和尿培养以排除其他感染源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 15,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未引用参考文献，比例未超过 30%，不触发扣分。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 16,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"病理生理学内容比例适中，未造成冗余，不触发扣分。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 17,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"回复结构清晰，符合临床逻辑，未出现 verbose 或组织混乱，不触发扣分。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 18,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型使用标准医学术语，未出现社会科学术语，不触发扣分。\"\n  }\n]"}, "error": null, "stage": null, "system_prompt": "You are a domain expert capable of delivering professional-grade responses in both English and 中文.\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. **Language**: Detect the question's language and respond entirely in that language. For Chinese, use natural, idiomatic professional Chinese — not translation-style. Never mix languages unless a term has no established translation.\n\n2. **Role**: If the question assigns a role, adopt it fully. If not, infer the appropriate expert identity from the scenario.\n\n3. **Scenario Focus**: Address the specific scenario directly. Do not provide generic domain overviews.\n\n4. **Factual Accuracy**: Use precise technical terminology, causal mechanisms, and quantitative specifics. Distinguish consensus from speculation.\n\n5. **Analytical Depth**: Decompose problems logically. Compare options with explicit dimensions and trade-offs. Explain \"why\" and \"how,\" not just \"what.\" Consider edge cases and real-world constraints.\n\n6. **Structure**: Use clear headings, numbered lists for sequences, bullets for parallel items, tables for multi-item comparisons. Lead with the key answer, then elaborate. End longer responses with a summary.\n\n7. **Instruction Following**: Address ALL sub-questions explicitly. Honor any specified constraints exactly.\n\n8. **Prohibitions**: Never fabricate data or citations. Never ignore parts of the question. Never be unnecessarily verbose. Never respond in the wrong language.", "user_prompt": "A 70-year-old woman has had abnormal vaginal discharge with malodor for the past 2 months, without vaginal bleeding, accompanied by lower abdominal discomfort. She presented to a local hospital; ultrasound showed separation of the endometrial line by 5 mm. She was admitted and developed cough on the day of admission; chest CT demonstrated bilateral lower-lobe pneumonia. After 3 days of intravenous moxifloxacin, she underwent hysteroscopic evaluation under intravenous anesthesia. Hysteroscopy revealed pyometra; after uterine cavity irrigation, dilation and curettage was performed. One hour postoperatively, she developed chills; temperature rose to 38.6°C, oxygen saturation fell to 90%, and heart rate was 100 beats/min. Please consider the causes of her fever and the additional laboratory tests and examinations that should be obtained.", "response": {"request_id": "omb-batch", "status": "completed", "session_id": "ses_3056df12effemqXRRzlnSDnKVB", "workspace": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/healthcare_and_medicine__6111__global/omb-batch", "system_prompt": "You are a domain expert capable of delivering professional-grade responses in both English and 中文.\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. **Language**: Detect the question's language and respond entirely in that language. For Chinese, use natural, idiomatic professional Chinese — not translation-style. Never mix languages unless a term has no established translation.\n\n2. **Role**: If the question assigns a role, adopt it fully. If not, infer the appropriate expert identity from the scenario.\n\n3. **Scenario Focus**: Address the specific scenario directly. Do not provide generic domain overviews.\n\n4. **Factual Accuracy**: Use precise technical terminology, causal mechanisms, and quantitative specifics. Distinguish consensus from speculation.\n\n5. **Analytical Depth**: Decompose problems logically. Compare options with explicit dimensions and trade-offs. Explain \"why\" and \"how,\" not just \"what.\" Consider edge cases and real-world constraints.\n\n6. **Structure**: Use clear headings, numbered lists for sequences, bullets for parallel items, tables for multi-item comparisons. Lead with the key answer, then elaborate. End longer responses with a summary.\n\n7. **Instruction Following**: Address ALL sub-questions explicitly. Honor any specified constraints exactly.\n\n8. **Prohibitions**: Never fabricate data or citations. Never ignore parts of the question. Never be unnecessarily verbose. Never respond in the wrong language.", "final_prompt": "A 70-year-old woman has had abnormal vaginal discharge with malodor for the past 2 months, without vaginal bleeding, accompanied by lower abdominal discomfort. She presented to a local hospital; ultrasound showed separation of the endometrial line by 5 mm. She was admitted and developed cough on the day of admission; chest CT demonstrated bilateral lower-lobe pneumonia. After 3 days of intravenous moxifloxacin, she underwent hysteroscopic evaluation under intravenous anesthesia. Hysteroscopy revealed pyometra; after uterine cavity irrigation, dilation and curettage was performed. One hour postoperatively, she developed chills; temperature rose to 38.6°C, oxygen saturation fell to 90%, and heart rate was 100 beats/min. Please consider the causes of her fever and the additional laboratory tests and examinations that should be obtained.", "session_data": {"scope_id": "e5ebb36b5ce0616d9d1736b843ef48e9ffc00c57", "session_id": "ses_3056df12effemqXRRzlnSDnKVB", "info": {"id": "ses_3056df12effemqXRRzlnSDnKVB", "version": "local", "scopeID": "e5ebb36b5ce0616d9d1736b843ef48e9ffc00c57", "directory": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/healthcare_and_medicine__6111__global/omb-batch", "title": "onemillion:healthcare_and_medicine/6111/global", "time": {"created": 1773730402001, "updated": 1773730402127}, "summary": {"additions": 0, "deletions": 0, "files": 0}}, "messages": [{"id": "msg_cfa920eec001E4RBLxWHrAiI2w", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa920eec001E4RBLxWHrAiI2w", "sessionID": "ses_3056df12effemqXRRzlnSDnKVB", "role": "user", "time": {"created": 1773730402028}, "summary": {"title": "Fever causes and necessary tests in postpartum pyometra", "diffs": []}, "agent": "synergy", "model": {"providerID": "sii-holos", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B"}}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa920eed001h2KxDnKYDP5QMA", "sessionID": "ses_3056df12effemqXRRzlnSDnKVB", "messageID": "msg_cfa920eec001E4RBLxWHrAiI2w", "type": "text", "text": "\"A 70-year-old woman has had abnormal vaginal discharge with malodor for the past 2 months, without vaginal bleeding, accompanied by lower abdominal discomfort. She presented to a local hospital; ultrasound showed separation of the endometrial line by 5 mm. She was admitted and developed cough on the day of admission; chest CT demonstrated bilateral lower-lobe pneumonia. After 3 days of intravenous moxifloxacin, she underwent hysteroscopic evaluation under intravenous anesthesia. Hysteroscopy revealed pyometra; after uterine cavity irrigation, dilation and curettage was performed. One hour postoperatively, she developed chills; temperature rose to 38.6°C, oxygen saturation fell to 90%, and heart rate was 100 beats/min. Please consider the causes of her fever and the additional laboratory tests and examinations that should be obtained.\"\n"}]}, {"id": "msg_cfa920f230014Ojp2AIbXU8i4Y", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa920f230014Ojp2AIbXU8i4Y", "sessionID": "ses_3056df12effemqXRRzlnSDnKVB", "role": "assistant", "time": {"created": 1773730402083, "completed": 1773730465560}, "parentID": "msg_cfa920eec001E4RBLxWHrAiI2w", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B", "providerID": "sii-holos", "mode": "synergy", "agent": "synergy", "path": {"cwd": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/healthcare_and_medicine__6111__global/omb-batch", "root": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/healthcare_and_medicine__6111__global/omb-batch"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 25856, "output": 1374, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "finish": "stop"}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa9212f1001i18skI