oning the validity of the assay kit.", "session_data": {"scope_id": "72610db978f5c0b425ff969ec3d9f1c236c7168c", "session_id": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "info": {"id": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "version": "local", "scopeID": "72610db978f5c0b425ff969ec3d9f1c236c7168c", "directory": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8479__global/omb-batch", "title": "onemillion:natural_science/8479/global", "time": {"created": 1773730535069, "updated": 1773730633591}, "summary": {"additions": 0, "deletions": 0, "files": 0}}, "messages": [{"id": "msg_cfa9416b0001h3a7u25hf0t1om", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa9416b0001h3a7u25hf0t1om", "sessionID": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "role": "user", "time": {"created": 1773730535088}, "summary": {"title": "Ensuring stable SETDB1 activity assay results", "diffs": []}, "agent": "synergy", "model": {"providerID": "sii-holos", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B"}}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa9416b1001gM8OP7grYdLUwx", "sessionID": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "messageID": "msg_cfa9416b0001h3a7u25hf0t1om", "type": "text", "text": "\"Existing studies indicate that SETDB1 is a critical histone lysine methyltransferase, primarily participating in key biological processes such as heterochromatin formation, transcriptional silencing, and genomic stability maintenance by catalyzing H3K9 trimethylation (H3K9me3) on histone H3. When employing the Promega MTase-Glo Universal Methyltransferase Assay system to detect SETDB1 enzymatic activity, I observed significant deviations in enzymatic activity assay data across multiple experiments, resulting in unstable outcomes. Given that the SETDB1 protein and substrate (full-length Histone H3) used in these experiments were purified from the same batch, please provide recommendations for the experimental protocol to ensure the stability of the enzymatic activity assay data, without changing the protein or substrate and without questioning the validity of the assay kit.\"\n"}]}, {"id": "msg_cfa9416e0001SJeOo107lwZQFG", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa9416e0001SJeOo107lwZQFG", "sessionID": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "role": "assistant", "time": {"created": 1773730535136, "completed": 1773730554856}, "parentID": "msg_cfa9416b0001h3a7u25hf0t1om", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B", "providerID": "sii-holos", "mode": "synergy", "agent": "synergy", "path": {"cwd": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8479__global/omb-batch", "root": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8479__global/omb-batch"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 25844, "output": 317, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "finish": "tool-calls"}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa941bb0001CpknONUGO1KgCR", "sessionID": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "messageID": "msg_cfa9416e0001SJeOo107lwZQFG", "type": "step-start", "snapshot": "4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904"}, {"id": "prt_cfa941bb1001tDo0kZeZoXvPQg", "sessionID": "ses_3056be963ffeccFb5xfI1q42n3", "messageID": "msg_cfa9416e0001SJeOo107lwZQFG", "type": "reasoning", "text": "This is a technical question about optimizing an enzymatic activity assay protocol for SETDB1, a histone methyltransferase. The user is experiencing data instability with the Promega MTase-Glo assay system and wants protocol recommendations without changing the protein/substrate or questioning the kit validity.\n\nLet me search for relevant information about:\n1. SETDB1 enzymatic activity assays\n2. MTase-Glo assay optimization\n3. Common sources of variability in methyltransferase assays\n4. Best practices for H3K9 methyltransferase activity measurements\n\nI should search for current protocols and troubleshooting guidance.", "time": {"start": 1773730536369, "end": 1773730554845}}, {"id": "prt_cfa942be70016yYp9FJisgwokt", "sessionID": "s