prt_cfa961b81001GXFK2x2vqd1UNQ", "sessionID": "ses_3056a8d14ffeI5s1BNL27a3ZpQ", "messageID": "msg_cfa9601f90013iGzmKJbPnO0gr", "type": "tool", "callID": "call_a15c5d189ff4494eba61b879", "tool": "websearch", "state": {"status": "error", "input": {"query": "protein buffer formulation screen design pH stabilizers surfactants sugars", "numResults": 8}, "error": "Error: Unable to connect. Is the computer able to access the url?", "time": {"start": 1773730668126, "end": 1773730668241}}}, {"id": "prt_cfa961ed2001zMVEN3g6ahxXLw", "sessionID": "ses_3056a8d14ffeI5s1BNL27a3ZpQ", "messageID": "msg_cfa9601f90013iGzmKJbPnO0gr", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "e60a15c6eeafbd0e7953a9e4d55aca2fb1f852ea", "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 49372, "output": 119, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}}]}, {"id": "msg_cfa961ef2001lHVfESVBAHkdPR", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa961ef2001lHVfESVBAHkdPR", "sessionID": "ses_3056a8d14ffeI5s1BNL27a3ZpQ", "role": "assistant", "time": {"created": 1773730668274, "completed": 1773730821779}, "parentID": "msg_cfa957302001C08s3MrGVLv1v1", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B", "providerID": "sii-holos", "mode": "synergy", "agent": "synergy", "path": {"cwd": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy", "root": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 49541, "output": 4140, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "finish": "stop"}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa96268c001Vj3zXooh2jXphd", "sessionID": "ses_3056a8d14ffeI5s1BNL27a3ZpQ", "messageID": "msg_cfa961ef2001lHVfESVBAHkdPR", "type": "step-start", "snapshot": "e60a15c6eeafbd0e7953a9e4d55aca2fb1f852ea"}, {"id": "prt_cfa96268d001mdiwwU3EMS368w", "sessionID": "ses_3056a8d14ffeI5s1BNL27a3ZpQ", "messageID": "msg_cfa961ef2001lHVfESVBAHkdPR", "type": "text", "text": "\n\nI see there are connectivity issues with web searches. Let me work with the information I've gathered from the arXiv papers and provide you with a comprehensive development proposal based on established protein biochemistry principles and the current scientific literature.\n\n---\n\n# **Ku Antigen In-House Development Proposal**\n\n## **Executive Summary**\n\nThis proposal outlines a rational strategy for the molecular construct design, protein expression, and preservation buffer formulation of the Ku antigen (Ku70/Ku80 heterodimer) for in vitro diagnostics and biological research applications. The approach integrates current best practices in recombinant protein production with evidence-based formulation science.\n\n---\n\n## **1. Molecular Construct Design**\n\n### **1.1 Target Selection and Antigen Rationale**\n\nThe Ku antigen is a heterodimeric complex consisting of Ku70 (≈70 kDa) and Ku80 (≈80 kDa) subunits that forms the DNA-binding component of the DNA-dependent protein kinase (DNA-PK) complex. For diagnostic applications, several considerations guide construct design:\n\n**Recommended Approach: Full-Length Heterodimer**\n\n| Subunit | UniProt Accession | Length | Key Domains |\n|---------|------------------|--------|-------------|\n| Ku70 | P12956 (human) | 609 aa | von Willebrand A domain, Ku core, SAP domain, C-terminal ARM domain |\n| Ku80 | P13010 (human) | 732 aa | von Willebrand A domain, Ku core, C-terminal DNA-PKcs interaction domain |\n\n**Rationale:**\n- Full-length heterodimer preserves conformational epitopes critical for autoantibody detection in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) and related autoimmune disorders\n- Both subunits required for proper folding and DNA-binding activity\n- Heterodimerization occurs co-translationally; co-expression essential\n\n### **1.2 Vector Construction Strategy**\n\n**Recommended: Dual-Vector or Bicistronic Expression System**\n\n**Option A: Two Separate Vectors (Recommended for Initial Development)**\n```\nVector 1: pET28a-Ku70-His6\n  - T7 promoter\n  - N-terminal 6×His tag (for purification)\n  - Kanamycin resistance\n  - E. coli codon-optimized sequence\n\nVector 2: pET22b-Ku80\n  - T7 promoter\n  - No tag (or C-terminal Flag tag for detection)\n  - Ampicillin resistance\n  - E. coli codon-optimized sequence\n```\n\n**Option B: Bicistronic Vector (For Stable Production)**\n```\npETDuet-1-Ku70/Ku80\n  - MCS1: Ku70-His6 (T7 promoter)\n  - MCS2: Ku80 (T7 promoter)\n  - Single antibiotic selection\n```\n\n**Critical Design Elements:**\n\n1. **Codon Optimization**: Essential for E. coli expression; use algorithms optimized for BL21(DE3)\n2. **Tag Placement**: \n   - His6 tag on Ku70 N-terminus (verified to not interfere with heterodimerization)\n   - Avoid tags on Ku80 C-terminus (required for DNA-PKcs interaction if functional assays needed)\n3. **Linker Considerations**: No artificial linker needed; native heterodimerization interface sufficient\n\n### **1.3 Truncated Constructs for Alternative Applications**\n\nIf full-length expression proves challenging:\n\n**Ku Core Domain Construct (Residues for Epitope Mapping)**\n- Ku70: residues 1-540 (core DNA-binding domain)\n- Ku80: residues 1-520 (core DNA-binding domain)\n- Retains major immunodominant epitopes\n- Higher solubility in bacterial systems\n\n---\n\n## **2. Protein Expression Strategy**\n\n### **2.1 Expression System Selection**\n\n**Primary Recommendation: E. coli BL21(DE3)**\n\n| Parameter | Rationale |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| **Host strain** | BL21(DE3) or Rosetta2(DE3) for enhanced codon usage |\n| **Growth temperature** | 18-20°C post-induction (critical for solubility) |\n| **Induction** | 0.1-0.5 mM IPTG at OD600 ≈ 0.6-0.8 |\n| **Induction time** | 16-20 h (overnight) |\n| **Media** | TB (Terrific Broth) or 2×YT for higher yields |\n\n**Alternative Systems (if E. coli fails):**\n- **Baculovirus/Sf9**: For proper eukaryotic folding and post-translational modifications\n- **HEK293F (transient)**: For small-scale functional validation\n- **CHO (stable)**: For GMP-grade production (long-term goal)\n\n### **2.2 Expression Protocol**\n\n**Step-by-Step Workflow:**\n\n```\n1. Transformation\n   - Co-transform both vectors into BL21(DE3)\n   - Plate on LB + Kan + Amp; incubate 37°C overnight\n\n2. Starter Culture\n   - Pick single colony into 10 mL LB + antibiotics\n   - Grow 37°C, 200 rpm, overnight\n\n3. Scale-Up\n   - Inoculate 1 L TB + antibiotics (1:100 dilution)\n   - Grow 37°C, 200 rpm, to OD600 = 0.6-0.8\n\n4. Induction\n   - Reduce temperature to 18°C\n   - Add IPTG to 0.2 mM final concentration\n   - Continue shaking 18-20 h at 18°C\n\n5. Harvest\n   - Centrifuge 4,000 × g, 15 min, 4°C\n   - Store pellet at -80°C or process immediately\n```\n\n### **2.3 Purification Strategy**\n\n**Multi-Step Purification Scheme:**\n\n**Step 1: Cell Lysis**\n```\nLysis Buffer:\n- 50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5\n- 300 mM NaCl\n- 10 mM imidazole\n- 1 mM PMSF\n- 1 mM DTT\n- 0.1% Triton X-100\n- Lysozyme (1 mg/mL)\n- DNase I (5 μg/mL) + MgCl2 (5 mM)\n```\n\n**Step 2: Ni-NTA Affinity Chromatography**\n- Equilibrate with lysis buffer\n- Load cleared lysate\n- Wash with 20-30 mM imidazole\n- Elute with 250-300 mM imidazole\n- **Critical**: Include heterodimerization partner in elution verification (Western blot for both subunits)\n\n**Step 3: Ion Exchange Chromatography (Optional)**\n- **Column**: HiTrap Q HP (anion exchange) or SP HP (cation exchange)\n- **Buffer A**: 20 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5, 50 mM NaCl\n- **Buffer B**: 20 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5, 1 M NaCl\n- **Gradient**: 0-50% B over 20 CV\n- Ku heterodimer typically elutes at 200-400 mM NaCl\n\n**Step 4: Size Exclusion Chromatography (SEC) - Essential**\n```\nColumn: Superdex 200 Increase 10/300 GL\nRunning Buffer:\n- 20 mM HEPES, pH 7.5\n- 150 mM NaCl\n- 1 mM DTT\n- 5% glycerol\n\nExpected elution: ~150 kDa peak (heterodimer)\n```\n\n**Quality Control:**\n- SDS-PAGE (Coomassie and Western)\n- SEC-MALS for molecular weight confirmation\n- DNA-binding assay (EMSA) for functional validation\n- Endotoxin removal if needed for cell-based assays\n\n---\n\n## **3. Proprietary Preservation Buffer Formulation**\n\n### **3.1 Formulation Design Principles**\n\nBased on recent advances in protein stabilization science (Doekhie et al., 2018; Miotto et al., 2023; Zajac et al., 2024), the following principles guide buffer design:\n\n**Key Stabilization Mechanisms:**\n1. **Preferential Exclusion**: Osmolytes excluded from protein surface stabilize native state\n2. **Hydrophobic Effect Modulation**: Arginine and amino acids modulate hydrophobic interactions\n3. **Glass Transition**: Sugars form amorphous glass matrix in frozen/dried state\n4. **pH Optimization**: Maintain distance from pI to maximize solubility\n\n### **3.2 Base Buffer System**\n\n**Recommended Starting Formulation:**\n\n```\nComponent              | Concentration | Function\n-----------------------|---------------|----------------------------------\nHEPES or Tris-HCl      | 20 mM         | pH buffering (pH 7.2-7.5)\nNaCl                   | 150 mM        | Ionic strength, osmolarity\nGlycerol               | 10-20% (v/v)  | Cryoprotectant, stabilizer\nTrehalose              | 100-200 mM    | Lyoprotectant, long-term stability\nL-Arginine-HCl         | 50-100 mM     | Suppresses aggregation (Zajac et al., 2024)\nDTT or TCEP            | 1-2 mM        | Prevents oxidation\nPolysorbate 20/80      | 0.01-0.02%    | Prevents surface adsorption\nEDTA                   | 0.5-1 mM      | Metal chelation (optional)\n```\n\n### **3.3 Formulation Screening Strategy**\n\n**High-Throughput Screening Approach:**\n\n**Phase 1: pH and Buffer Type Screen**\n| Buffer | pH Range |\n|--------|----------|\n| Sodium acetate | 5.0, 5.5, 6.0 |\n| Histidine | 6.0, 6.5, 7.0 |\n| HEPES | 7.0, 7.5, 8.0 |\n| Tris-HCl | 7.5, 8.0, 8.5 |\n| Glycyl-glycine | 8.0, 8.5, 9.0 |\n\n**Phase 2: Stabilizer Matrix Screen**\n\nTest combinations of:\n- **Sugars**: Trehalose (0, 100, 200, 300 mM), Sucrose (0, 100, 200 mM)\n- **Polyols**: Glycerol (0, 5, 10, 20%), Sorbitol (0, 100, 200 mM)\n- **Amino Acids**: Arginine (0, 50, 100, 150 mM), Glycine (0, 100, 200 mM)\n- **Surfactants**: Polysorbate 20 (0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02%), Polysorbate 80 (same)\n\n**Phase 3: Accelerated Stability Testing**\n\n| Condition | Duration | Readout |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| 4°C | 1, 2, 4, 8 weeks | SEC, activity assay |\n| 25°C | 1, 2, 4 weeks | SEC, activity assay |\n| 37°C | 1, 2, 4 weeks | SEC, activity assay |\n| -20°C (5 freeze-thaw cycles) | 2 weeks | SEC, visual inspection |\n| -80°C | 1, 3, 6 months | SEC, activity assay |\n\n**Analytical Readouts:**\n- **SEC-HPLC**: Monomer/dimer/aggregate content\n- **DSF (Differential Scanning Fluorimetry)**: Tm shift\n- **DLS (Dynamic Light Scattering)**: Hydrodynamic radius, polydispersity\n- **Functional Assay**: DNA-binding (EMSA) or antibody recognition (ELISA)\n- **Visual**: Particulate formation, color change, precipitation\n\n### **3.4 Optimized Formulation Recommendations**\n\n**Short-Term Storage (4°C, 1-4 weeks):**\n```\n- 20 mM HEPES, pH 7.5\n- 150 mM NaCl\n- 10% glycerol\n- 1 mM DTT\n- 0.01% Polysorbate 20\n- 50 mM arginine-HCl\n```\n\n**Long-Term Storage (-80°C, 6-24 months):**\n```\n- 20 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5\n- 150 mM NaCl\n- 20% glycerol\n- 200 mM trehalose\n- 1 mM TCEP\n- 0.02% Polysorbate 80\n- 100 mM arginine-HCl\n```\n\n**Lyophilized Formulation (if needed):**\n```\n- 20 mM Histidine, pH 6.5\n- 300 mM trehalose\n- 2% mannitol (bulking agent)\n- 0.02% Polysorbate 20\n- Reconstitute with sterile water to original concentration\n```\n\n---\n\n## **4. Critical Success Factors and Risk Mitigation**\n\n### **4.1 Technical Risks**\n\n| Risk | Mitigation Strategy |\n|------|---------------------|\n| **Low solubility in E. coli** | Test at 16-18°C; use chaperone co-expression (pGro7, pKJE7); consider SUMO/MBP fusion |\n| **Heterodimer instability** | Co-purify both subunits; verify by SEC-MALS and co-IP |\n| **Aggregation during purification** | Include 50-100 mM arginine in all buffers; keep protein concentration <5 mg/mL |\n| **Loss of DNA-binding activity** | Minimize freeze-thaw; include 5% glycerol; avoid >pH 8.5 |\n| **Endotoxin contamination** | Use endotoxin-free reagents; include polymyxin B column if needed for cell-based assays |\n\n### **4.2 Quality Control Specifications**\n\n| Parameter | Acceptance Criteria |\n|-----------|---------------------|\n| **Purity (SDS-PAGE)** | >95% |\n| **Heterodimer content (SEC)** | >90% |\n| **Endotoxin** | <1 EU/mg (for cell-based assays) |\n| **DNA-binding (EMSA)** | Specific band shift with Ku consensus sequence |\n| **Antibody recognition (ELISA)** | Positive with anti-Ku70/Ku80 mAbs; positive with SLE patient sera |\n| **Concentration** | 1-5 mg/mL (adjustable based on application) |\n\n---\n\n## **5. Timeline and Milestones**\n\n| Phase | Duration | Deliverables |\n|-------|----------|--------------|\n| **Construct Design & Cloning** | 4-6 weeks | Verified expression plasmids |\n| **Expression Screening** | 3-4 weeks | Optimal expression conditions |\n| **Purification Development** | 4-6 weeks | Robust purification protocol |\n| **Buffer Formulation Screen** | 6-8 weeks | Lead formulation(s) |\n| **Stability Testing** | 8-12 weeks | Stability data, shelf-life prediction |\n| **Analytical Validation** | 4-6 weeks | QC methods, specifications |\n\n**Total Timeline: 6-9 months**\n\n---\n\n## **6. References and Supporting Literature**\n\n1. **Doekhie, A. et al.** (2018). A solid approach to biopharmaceutical stabilisation. *arXiv:1811.12291*. Demonstrates ensilication technology for ambient-temperature protein storage.\n\n2. **Miotto, M. et al.** (2023). Osmolyte-Induced Protein Stability Changes Explained by Graph Theory. *arXiv:2305.05038*. Mechanistic insights into osmolyte-protein interactions.\n\n3. **Zajac, J.W.P. et al.** (2024). Impact of Co-Excipient Selection on Hydrophobic Polymer Folding. *arXiv:2407.00885*. Rational design rules for arginine-based formulations.\n\n4. **Zweng, S. et al.** (2023). Simplifying recombinant protein production: Combining Golden Gate cloning with standardized purification. *arXiv:2310.06456*. Streamlined protein production workflows.\n\n5. **Mao, T. et al.** (2024). Amino Acids Stabilizing Effect on Protein and Colloidal Dispersions. *arXiv:2404.11574*. Quantitative framework for amino acid stabilization.\n\n---\n\n## **7. Conclusions and Next Steps**\n\nThis proposal provides a comprehensive, evidence-based approach to in-house Ku antigen development. Key recommendations include:\n\n1. **Pursue full-length heterodimer expression** in E. coli BL21(DE3) with dual-vector system\n2. **Implement multi-step purification** with SEC as critical quality control step\n3. **Adopt rational buffer design** based on preferential exclusion and hydrophobic modulation principles\n4. **Screen formulations systematically** using accelerated stability testing\n5. **Validate with functional and immunological assays** relevant to diagnostic applications\n\n**Immediate Next Steps:**\n- Order codon-optimized gene fragments for Ku70 and Ku80\n- Clone into pET28a and pET22b vectors\n- Begin small-scale expression trials at 18°C and 25°C\n- Prepare initial buffer screen with 12-16 conditions\n\nThis development program will establish a robust, cost-effective alternative to commercial sources while maintaining the quality and reliability required for diagnostic and research applications.", "time": {"start": 1773730821752, "end": 1773730821752}}, {"id": "prt_cfa98767a001ftMLfhCnieE8ee", "sessionID": "ses_3056a8d14ffeI5s1BNL27a3ZpQ", "messageID": "msg_cfa961ef2001lHVfESVBAHkdPR", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "stop", "snapshot": "e60a15c6eeafbd0e7953a9e4d55aca2fb1f852ea", "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 49541, "output": 4140, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}}]}]}, "result": {"answer": "I see there are connectivity issues with web searches. Let me work with the information I've gathered from the arXiv papers and provide you with a comprehensive development proposal based on established protein biochemistry principles and the current scientific literature.\n\n---\n\n# **Ku Antigen In-House Development Proposal**\n\n## **Executive Summary**\n\nThis proposal outlines a rational strategy for the molecular construct design, protein expression, and preservation buffer formulation of the Ku antigen (Ku70/Ku80 heterodimer) for in vitro diagnostics and biological research applications. The approach integrates current best practices in recombinant protein production with evidence-based formulation science.\n\n---\n\n## **1. Molecular Construct Design**\n\n### **1.1 Target Selection and Antigen Rationale**\n\nThe Ku antigen is a heterodimeric complex consisting of Ku70 (≈70 kDa) and Ku80 (≈80 kDa) subunits that forms the DNA-binding component of the DNA-dependent protein kinase (DNA-PK) complex. For diagnostic applications, several considerations guide construct design:\n\n**Recommended Approach: Full-Length Heterodimer**\n\n| Subunit | UniProt Accession | Length | Key Domains |\n|---------|------------------|--------|-------------|\n| Ku70 | P12956 (human) | 609 aa | von Willebrand A domain, Ku core, SAP domain, C-terminal ARM domain |\n| Ku80 | P13010 (human) | 732 aa | von Willebrand A domain, Ku core, C-terminal DNA-PKcs interaction domain |\n\n**Rationale:**\n- Full-length heterodimer preserves conformational epitopes critical for autoantibody detection in systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) and related autoimmune disorders\n- Both subunits required for proper folding and DNA-binding activity\n- Heterodimerization occurs co-translationally; co-expression essential\n\n### **1.2 Vector Construction Strategy**\n\n**Recommended: Dual-Vector or Bicistronic Expression System**\n\n**Option A: Two Separate Vectors (Recommended for Initial Development)**\n```\nVector 1: pET28a-Ku70-His6\n  - T7 promoter\n  - N-terminal 6×His tag (for purification)\n  - Kanamycin resistance\n  - E. coli codon-optimized sequence\n\nVector 2: pET22b-Ku80\n  - T7 promoter\n  - No tag (or C-terminal Flag tag for detection)\n  - Ampicillin resistance\n  - E. coli codon-optimized sequence\n```\n\n**Option B: Bicistronic Vector (For Stable Production)**\n```\npETDuet-1-Ku70/Ku80\n  - MCS1: Ku70-His6 (T7 promoter)\n  - MCS2: Ku80 (T7 promoter)\n  - Single antibiotic selection\n```\n\n**Critical Design Elements:**\n\n1. **Codon Optimization**: Essential for E. coli expression; use algorithms optimized for BL21(DE3)\n2. **Tag Placement**: \n   - His6 tag on Ku70 N-terminus (verified to not interfere with heterodimerization)\n   - Avoid tags on Ku80 C-terminus (required for DNA-PKcs interaction if functional assays needed)\n3. **Linker Considerations**: No artificial linker needed; native heterodimerization interface sufficient\n\n### **1.3 Truncated Constructs for Alternative Applications**\n\nIf full-length expression proves challenging:\n\n**Ku Core Domain Construct (Residues for Epitope Mapping)**\n- Ku70: residues 1-540 (core DNA-binding domain)\n- Ku80: residues 1-520 (core DNA-binding domain)\n- Retains major immunodominant epitopes\n- Higher solubility in bacterial systems\n\n---\n\n## **2. Protein Expression Strategy**\n\n### **2.1 Expression System Selection**\n\n**Primary Recommendation: E. coli BL21(DE3)**\n\n| Parameter | Rationale |\n|-----------|-----------|\n| **Host strain** | BL21(DE3) or Rosetta2(DE3) for enhanced codon usage |\n| **Growth temperature** | 18-20°C post-induction (critical for solubility) |\n| **Induction** | 0.1-0.5 mM IPTG at OD600 ≈ 0.6-0.8 |\n| **Induction time** | 16-20 h (overnight) |\n| **Media** | TB (Terrific Broth) or 2×YT for higher yields |\n\n**Alternative Systems (if E. coli fails):**\n- **Baculovirus/Sf9**: For proper eukaryotic folding and post-translational modifications\n- **HEK293F (transient)**: For small-scale functional validation\n- **CHO (stable)**: For GMP-grade production (long-term goal)\n\n### **2.2 Expression Protocol**\n\n**Step-by-Step Workflow:**\n\n```\n1. Transformation\n   - Co-transform both vectors into BL21(DE3)\n   - Plate on LB + Kan + Amp; incubate 37°C overnight\n\n2. Starter Culture\n   - Pick single colony into 10 mL LB + antibiotics\n   - Grow 37°C, 200 rpm, overnight\n\n3. Scale-Up\n   - Inoculate 1 L TB + antibiotics (1:100 dilution)\n   - Grow 37°C, 200 rpm, to OD600 = 0.6-0.8\n\n4. Induction\n   - Reduce temperature to 18°C\n   - Add IPTG to 0.2 mM final concentration\n   - Continue shaking 18-20 h at 18°C\n\n5. Harvest\n   - Centrifuge 4,000 × g, 15 min, 4°C\n   - Store pellet at -80°C or process immediately\n```\n\n### **2.3 Purification Strategy**\n\n**Multi-Step Purification Scheme:**\n\n**Step 1: Cell Lysis**\n```\nLysis Buffer:\n- 50 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5\n- 300 mM NaCl\n- 10 mM imidazole\n- 1 mM PMSF\n- 1 mM DTT\n- 0.1% Triton X-100\n- Lysozyme (1 mg/mL)\n- DNase I (5 μg/mL) + MgCl2 (5 mM)\n```\n\n**Step 2: Ni-NTA Affinity Chromatography**\n- Equilibrate with lysis buffer\n- Load cleared lysate\n- Wash with 20-30 mM imidazole\n- Elute with 250-300 mM imidazole\n- **Critical**: Include heterodimerization partner in elution verification (Western blot for both subunits)\n\n**Step 3: Ion Exchange Chromatography (Optional)**\n- **Column**: HiTrap Q HP (anion exchange) or SP HP (cation exchange)\n- **Buffer A**: 20 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5, 50 mM NaCl\n- **Buffer B**: 20 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5, 1 M NaCl\n- **Gradient**: 0-50% B over 20 CV\n- Ku heterodimer typically elutes at 200-400 mM NaCl\n\n**Step 4: Size Exclusion Chromatography (SEC) - Essential**\n```\nColumn: Superdex 200 Increase 10/300 GL\nRunning Buffer:\n- 20 mM HEPES, pH 7.5\n- 150 mM NaCl\n- 1 mM DTT\n- 5% glycerol\n\nExpected elution: ~150 kDa peak (heterodimer)\n```\n\n**Quality Control:**\n- SDS-PAGE (Coomassie and Western)\n- SEC-MALS for molecular weight confirmation\n- DNA-binding assay (EMSA) for functional validation\n- Endotoxin removal if needed for cell-based assays\n\n---\n\n## **3. Proprietary Preservation Buffer Formulation**\n\n### **3.1 Formulation Design Principles**\n\nBased on recent advances in protein stabilization science (Doekhie et al., 2018; Miotto et al., 2023; Zajac et al., 2024), the following principles guide buffer design:\n\n**Key Stabilization Mechanisms:**\n1. **Preferential Exclusion**: Osmolytes excluded from protein surface stabilize native state\n2. **Hydrophobic Effect Modulation**: Arginine and amino acids modulate hydrophobic interactions\n3. **Glass Transition**: Sugars form amorphous glass matrix in frozen/dried state\n4. **pH Optimization**: Maintain distance from pI to maximize solubility\n\n### **3.2 Base Buffer System**\n\n**Recommended Starting Formulation:**\n\n```\nComponent              | Concentration | Function\n-----------------------|---------------|----------------------------------\nHEPES or Tris-HCl      | 20 mM         | pH buffering (pH 7.2-7.5)\nNaCl                   | 150 mM        | Ionic strength, osmolarity\nGlycerol               | 10-20% (v/v)  | Cryoprotectant, stabilizer\nTrehalose              | 100-200 mM    | Lyoprotectant, long-term stability\nL-Arginine-HCl         | 50-100 mM     | Suppresses aggregation (Zajac et al., 2024)\nDTT or TCEP            | 1-2 mM        | Prevents oxidation\nPolysorbate 20/80      | 0.01-0.02%    | Prevents surface adsorption\nEDTA                   | 0.5-1 mM      | Metal chelation (optional)\n```\n\n### **3.3 Formulation Screening Strategy**\n\n**High-Throughput Screening Approach:**\n\n**Phase 1: pH and Buffer Type Screen**\n| Buffer | pH Range |\n|--------|----------|\n| Sodium acetate | 5.0, 5.5, 6.0 |\n| Histidine | 6.0, 6.5, 7.0 |\n| HEPES | 7.0, 7.5, 8.0 |\n| Tris-HCl | 7.5, 8.0, 8.5 |\n| Glycyl-glycine | 8.0, 8.5, 9.0 |\n\n**Phase 2: Stabilizer Matrix Screen**\n\nTest combinations of:\n- **Sugars**: Trehalose (0, 100, 200, 300 mM), Sucrose (0, 100, 200 mM)\n- **Polyols**: Glycerol (0, 5, 10, 20%), Sorbitol (0, 100, 200 mM)\n- **Amino Acids**: Arginine (0, 50, 100, 150 mM), Glycine (0, 100, 200 mM)\n- **Surfactants**: Polysorbate 20 (0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02%), Polysorbate 80 (same)\n\n**Phase 3: Accelerated Stability Testing**\n\n| Condition | Duration | Readout |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| 4°C | 1, 2, 4, 8 weeks | SEC, activity assay |\n| 25°C | 1, 2, 4 weeks | SEC, activity assay |\n| 37°C | 1, 2, 4 weeks | SEC, activity assay |\n| -20°C (5 freeze-thaw cycles) | 2 weeks | SEC, visual inspection |\n| -80°C | 1, 3, 6 months | SEC, activity assay |\n\n**Analytical Readouts:**\n- **SEC-HPLC**: Monomer/dimer/aggregate content\n- **DSF (Differential Scanning Fluorimetry)**: Tm shift\n- **DLS (Dynamic Light Scattering)**: Hydrodynamic radius, polydispersity\n- **Functional Assay**: DNA-binding (EMSA) or antibody recognition (ELISA)\n- **Visual**: Particulate formation, color change, precipitation\n\n### **3.4 Optimized Formulation Recommendations**\n\n**Short-Term Storage (4°C, 1-4 weeks):**\n```\n- 20 mM HEPES, pH 7.5\n- 150 mM NaCl\n- 10% glycerol\n- 1 mM DTT\n- 0.01% Polysorbate 20\n- 50 mM arginine-HCl\n```\n\n**Long-Term Storage (-80°C, 6-24 months):**\n```\n- 20 mM Tris-HCl, pH 7.5\n- 150 mM NaCl\n- 20% glycerol\n- 200 mM trehalose\n- 1 mM TCEP\n- 0.02% Polysorbate 80\n- 100 mM arginine-HCl\n```\n\n**Lyophilized Formulation (if needed):**\n```\n- 20 mM Histidine, pH 6.5\n- 300 mM trehalose\n- 2% mannitol (bulking agent)\n- 0.02% Polysorbate 20\n- Reconstitute with sterile water to original concentration\n```\n\n---\n\n## **4. Critical Success Factors and Risk Mitigation**\n\n### **4.1 Technical Risks**\n\n| Risk | Mitigation Strategy |\n|------|---------------------|\n| **Low solubility in E. coli** | Test at 16-18°C; use chaperone co-expression (pGro7, pKJE7); consider SUMO/MBP fusion |\n| **Heterodimer instability** | Co-purify both subunits; verify by SEC-MALS and co-IP |\n| **Aggregation during purification** | Include 50-100 mM arginine in all buffers; keep protein concentration <5 mg/mL |\n| **Loss of DNA-binding activity** | Minimize freeze-thaw; include 5% glycerol; avoid >pH 8.5 |\n| **Endotoxin contamination** | Use endotoxin-free reagents; include polymyxin B column if needed for cell-based assays |\n\n### **4.2 Quality Control Specifications**\n\n| Parameter | Acceptance Criteria |\n|-----------|---------------------|\n| **Purity (SDS-PAGE)** | >95% |\n| **Heterodimer content (SEC)** | >90% |\n| **Endotoxin** | <1 EU/mg (for cell-based assays) |\n| **DNA-binding (EMSA)** | Specific band shift with Ku consensus sequence |\n| **Antibody recognition (ELISA)** | Positive with anti-Ku70/Ku80 mAbs; positive with SLE patient sera |\n| **Concentration** | 1-5 mg/mL (adjustable based on application) |\n\n---\n\n## **5. Timeline and Milestones**\n\n| Phase | Duration | Deliverables |\n|-------|----------|--------------|\n| **Construct Design & Cloning** | 4-6 weeks | Verified expression plasmids |\n| **Expression Screening** | 3-4 weeks | Optimal expression conditions |\n| **Purification Development** | 4-6 weeks | Robust purification protocol |\n| **Buffer Formulation Screen** | 6-8 weeks | Lead formulation(s) |\n| **Stability Testing** | 8-12 weeks | Stability data, shelf-life prediction |\n| **Analytical Validation** | 4-6 weeks | QC methods, specifications |\n\n**Total Timeline: 6-9 months**\n\n---\n\n## **6. References and Supporting Literature**\n\n1. **Doekhie, A. et al.** (2018). A solid approach to biopharmaceutical stabilisation. *arXiv:1811.12291*. Demonstrates ensilication technology for ambient-temperature protein storage.\n\n2. **Miotto, M. et al.** (2023). Osmolyte-Induced Protein Stability Changes Explained by Graph Theory. *arXiv:2305.05038*. Mechanistic insights into osmolyte-protein interactions.\n\n3. **Zajac, J.W.P. et al.** (2024). Impact of Co-Excipient Selection on Hydrophobic Polymer Folding. *arXiv:2407.00885*. Rational design rules for arginine-based formulations.\n\n4. **Zweng, S. et al.** (2023). Simplifying recombinant protein production: Combining Golden Gate cloning with standardized purification. *arXiv:2310.06456*. Streamlined protein production workflows.\n\n5. **Mao, T. et al.** (2024). Amino Acids Stabilizing Effect on Protein and Colloidal Dispersions. *arXiv:2404.11574*. Quantitative framework for amino acid stabilization.\n\n---\n\n## **7. Conclusions and Next Steps**\n\nThis proposal provides a comprehensive, evidence-based approach to in-house Ku antigen development. Key recommendations include:\n\n1. **Pursue full-length heterodimer expression** in E. coli BL21(DE3) with dual-vector system\n2. **Implement multi-step purification** with SEC as critical quality control step\n3. **Adopt rational buffer design** based on preferential exclusion and hydrophobic modulation principles\n4. **Screen formulations systematically** using accelerated stability testing\n5. **Validate with functional and immunological assays** relevant to diagnostic applications\n\n**Immediate Next Steps:**\n- Order codon-optimized gene fragments for Ku70 and Ku80\n- Clone into pET28a and pET22b vectors\n- Begin small-scale expression trials at 18°C and 25°C\n- Prepare initial buffer screen with 12-16 conditions\n\nThis development program will establish a robust, cost-effective alternative to commercial sources while maintaining the quality and reliability required for diagnostic and research applications.", "case_id": 6697, "language": "global", "tags": {"topics": ["Natural Sciences", "Biology", "Molecular and Cell Biology"], "time_sensitivity": {"time_sensitivity": "Time-agnostic", "year_month": "NA", "day": "NA"}}, "rubric_count": 18}, "metrics": {"solve_time_seconds": 200.1, "tokens": {"input": 155646, "output": 4794, "total": 160440}, "cost": 0.0, "step_count": 4}, "error": ""}}
{"task_id": "natural_science/5683/cn", "answer": "arXiv 的搜索结果没有直接匹配这个反应。让我基于有机合成知识来分析这个反应。\n\n根据您提供的反应条件：\n- **反应物**：双(4-甲氧基苯基)胺 + 2-氧代-2-苯基乙醛（苯甲酰甲醛）+ 苯硼酸\n- **催化剂**：Cu(OTFA)₂·xH₂O（三氟乙酸铜）\n- **溶剂**：1,2-二氯乙烷，80°C\n\n这是一个典型的**三组分偶联反应**，属于**Petasis 反应**（或称 Petasis 硼酸-Mannich 反应）的变体。让我详细分析：\n\n## 产物 A 的结构与 IUPAC 名称\n\n这个反应是**α-酮醛、二芳胺和芳基硼酸的三组分偶联**，产物是**α-氨基酮**类化合物。\n\n**反应过程**：\n1. 2-氧代-2-苯基乙醛（Ph-CO-CHO）的醛基与双(4-甲氧基苯基)胺缩合形成亚胺中间体\n2. 苯硼酸对亚胺进行亲核加成（铜催化活化）\n3. 最终得到α-氨基酮\n\n**产物 A 的结构**：\n```\n                    O\n                    ||\nPh - C - CH - N(4-MeO-Ph)₂\n         |\n         Ph\n```\n\n**IUPAC 名称**：\n**2-(双(4-甲氧基苯基)氨基)-1,2-二苯基乙酮**\n英文：*2-(bis(4-methoxyphenyl)amino)-1,2-diphenylethanone*\n\n---\n\n## 预期的波谱数据\n\n### ¹H NMR (预计, 400 MHz, CDCl₃)\n\n| 化学位移 (δ, ppm) | 积分 | 裂分 | 归属 |\n|-------------------|------|------|------|\n| ~7.80-7.75 | 2H | d | 苯甲酰基邻位 H (与羰基共轭) |\n| ~7.50-7.20 | 8H | m | 两个苯基的芳香 H |\n| ~6.90-6.80 | 4H | d | 4-甲氧基苯基的芳香 H (邻位到 N) |\n| ~6.70-6.60 | 4H | d | 4-甲氧基苯基的芳香 H (邻位到 OMe) |\n| ~6.50 | 1H | s | CH (手性中心，连接 N 和 Ph) |\n| ~3.75 | 6H | s | 两个 OCH₃ |\n\n### ¹³C NMR (预计, 100 MHz, CDCl₃)\n\n| 化学位移 (δ, ppm) | 归属 |\n|-------------------|------|\n| ~195-200 | C=O (酮羰基) |\n| ~155-157 | C-O (甲氧基连接的碳) |\n| ~140-145 | 季碳 (与 N 相连的苯环 ipso 位) |\n| ~135-138 | 苯基季碳 (连接 CH) |\n| ~128-133 | 芳香 CH (多个) |\n| ~114-115 | 甲氧基苯环的芳香 CH |\n| ~65-70 | CH (手性中心) |\n| ~55-56 | OCH₃ |\n\n### DEPT 谱\n\n- **DEPT-135**：\n  - **正信号**（CH, CH₃）：~55 ppm (OCH₃), ~65 ppm (CH), 所有芳香 CH\n  - **负信号**（CH₂）：无（该分子没有 CH₂）\n  - **无信号**（季碳）：C=O (~195 ppm), C-O (~155 ppm), 季芳香碳\n\n- **DEPT-90**：\n  - 仅显示 CH：~65 ppm (手性 CH), 所有芳香 CH\n\n### ESI-MS (电喷雾电离质谱)\n\n**分子式**：C₂₈H₂₅NO₃  \n**分子量**：423.18 g/mol\n\n- **[M+H]⁺**：m/z = 424.2\n- **[M+Na]⁺**：m/z = 446.2\n- **[M+K]⁺**：m/z = 462.1\n\n---\n\n## 苯硼酸在反应中的作用\n\n苯硼酸在这个反应中扮演**亲核试剂**的角色，具体作用如下：\n\n### 1. **作为碳亲核试剂**\n苯硼酸中的苯基通过铜催化被活化，对亚胺中间体进行亲核加成，形成新的 C-C 键。\n\n### 2. **反应优势**\n- **温和性**：相比有机锂或格氏试剂，硼酸更稳定、更易处理\n- **选择性**：只与活化的亚胺反应，不与其他官能团反应\n- **原子经济性**：硼酸副产物无害\n\n---\n\n## 反应机理\n\n这是一个**铜催化的三组分 Petasis-type 反应**，可能的机理如下：\n\n```\n步骤 1: 亚胺形成\n                    OH\n                    |\nPh-CO-CHO + HN(Ar)₂ → Ph-CO-CH=N(Ar)₂ + H₂O\n(Ar = 4-MeO-Ph)\n\n步骤 2: 铜催化剂活化硼酸\nPh-B(OH)₂ + Cu(II) → [Ph-Cu(II)-B(OH)₂] 活性络合物\n\n步骤 3: 转金属化\n[Ph-Cu(II)-B(OH)₂] → Ph-Cu(III) 或 Ph-Cu(I) 活性物种\n\n步骤 4: 对亚胺的亲核加成\n                    O                    O\n                    ||                   ||\nPh-CO-CH=N(Ar)₂ + Ph-Cu → Ph-CO-CH-N(Ar)₂\n                              |\n                              Ph\n\n步骤 5: 质子化/产物释放\n                    O\n                    ||\nPh-CO-CH-N(Ar)₂ + H⁺ → 产物 A + Cu 催化剂再生\n         |\n         Ph\n```\n\n### 详细机理说明：\n\n1. **亚胺形成**（缩合）\n   - 2-氧代-2-苯基乙醛的醛基与双(4-甲氧基苯基)胺的氨基发生缩合\n   - 失去一分子水，形成亚胺（席夫碱）中间体\n   - 酮羰基保持不变（酮的反应性低于醛）\n\n2. **铜催化剂活化**\n   - Cu(II) 与苯硼酸配位，形成有机铜物种\n   - 可能经过转金属化生成 Ph-Cu(III) 或 Ph-Cu(I) 活性中间体\n\n3. **亲核加成**\n   - 活化的苯基对亚胺的 C=N 双键进行亲核进攻\n   - 这是反应的决速步\n   - 铜同时活化亚胺（作为路易斯酸）和苯硼酸（转金属化）\n\n4. **产物形成与催化剂再生**\n   - 加合物质子化，释放产物\n   - 铜催化剂再生，进入下一个催化循环\n\n### 反应的关键特点：\n\n- **区域选择性**：反应只发生在醛基位置，酮羰基不参与\n- **立体化学**：生成手性中心，但非手性条件下得到外消旋体\n- **铜的作用**：路易斯酸活化 + 转金属化媒介\n\n---\n\n## 总结\n\n| 项目 | 内容 |\n|------|------|\n| **产物 A** | 2-(双(4-甲氧基苯基)氨基)-1,2-二苯基乙酮 |\n| **分子式** | C₂₈H₂₅NO₃ |\n| **ESI-MS [M+H]⁺** | m/z 424.2 |\n| **关键 ¹H NMR** | δ ~6.5 (s, 1H, CH), ~3.75 (s, 6H, OMe) |\n| **关键 ¹³C NMR** | δ ~195 (C=O), ~65 (CH) |\n| **苯硼酸作用** | 提供苯基亲核试剂，形成新的 C-C 键 |\n| **反应类型** | 铜催化三组分 Petasis-type 偶联 |\n\n如果您需要更详细的机理图或实验验证建议，请告诉我！", "score": {"rubric_results": [{"rubric_number": 1, "weight": 8, "met": false, "reason": "模型给出的分子式为 C₂₈H₂₅NO₃，与评分标准要求的 C₂₈H₂₃NO₃ 不符。"}, {"rubric_number": 2, "weight": 10, "met": false, "reason": "模型给出的 IUPAC 名称为氨基酮类化合物，与评分标准要求的吲哚啉酮结构名称不一致。"}, {"rubric_number": 3, "weight": 6, "met": true, "reason": "模型在 1H NMR 表格中明确列出了两个单峰信号（~6.50 ppm 和 ~3.75 ppm）。"}, {"rubric_number": 4, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型仅列出 1 个低于 6.0 ppm 的信号（3.75 ppm），未指出有 2 个信号。"}, {"rubric_number": 5, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型表格中高于 6.0 ppm 的氢原子积分总和为 19H，与评分标准要求的 17H 不符。"}, {"rubric_number": 6, "weight": 8, "met": false, "reason": "模型未明确说明 13C NMR 谱图包含 22 个无重叠信号，仅列出了化学位移范围。"}, {"rubric_number": 7, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型碳谱数据中仅列出 2 组低于 100 ppm 的信号，未列出 3 个。"}, {"rubric_number": 8, "weight": 6, "met": true, "reason": "模型碳谱数据中包含~195-200 ppm 的信号，符合高于 180 ppm 的描述。"}, {"rubric_number": 9, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型回复中未提及 DEPT-45 谱图及其信号数量。"}, {"rubric_number": 10, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型未指出 DEPT-90 谱图包含 15 个不同的信号。"}, {"rubric_number": 11, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型未指出 DEPT-135 谱图结果有 13 个不同的正信号。"}, {"rubric_number": 12, "weight": 8, "met": false, "reason": "模型给出的 [M+H]⁺ m/z 为 424.2，不在评分标准要求的 421-423 区间内。"}, {"rubric_number": 13, "weight": 4, "met": false, "reason": "模型虽列出数据，但未在文本中对高场和低场区的质子分布特征进行逻辑区分和分析。"}, {"rubric_number": 14, "weight": 4, "met": true, "reason": "模型通过识别~195-200 ppm 信号，正确分析指出了酮羰基的存在。"}, {"rubric_number": 15, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型使用的化学术语、单位符号及分子式书写规范准确。"}, {"rubric_number": 16, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型完整覆盖了用户请求的 NMR、DEPT 和 ESI-MS 三类测试数据。"}, {"rubric_number": 17, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "模型提供的机理和硼酸作用是对用户明确提问的回答，不属于无关冗余内容。"}, {"rubric_number": 18, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "波谱数据使用了表格和列表格式，排版清晰，可读性好。"}, {"rubric_number": 19, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "模型在 1H NMR 部分明确提供了氘代试剂 CDCl₃。"}, {"rubric_number": 20, "weight": -5, "met": true, "reason": "模型回复中确实未提供柱层析洗脱剂极性（PE : DCM = 3:1）的信息。"}], "score": 17, "max_score": 93, "raw_response": "[\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型给出的分子式为 C₂₈H₂₅NO₃，与评分标准要求的 C₂₈H₂₃NO₃ 不符。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 2,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型给出的 IUPAC 名称为氨基酮类化合物，与评分标准要求的吲哚啉酮结构名称不一致。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 3,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在 1H NMR 表格中明确列出了两个单峰信号（~6.50 ppm 和 ~3.75 ppm）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 4,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型仅列出 1 个低于 6.0 ppm 的信号（3.75 ppm），未指出有 2 个信号。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 5,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型表格中高于 6.0 ppm 的氢原子积分总和为 19H，与评分标准要求的 17H 不符。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 6,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未明确说明 13C NMR 谱图包含 22 个无重叠信号，仅列出了化学位移范围。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 7,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型碳谱数据中仅列出 2 组低于 100 ppm 的信号，未列出 3 个。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 8,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型碳谱数据中包含~195-200 ppm 的信号，符合高于 180 ppm 的描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 9,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型回复中未提及 DEPT-45 谱图及其信号数量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 10,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未指出 DEPT-90 谱图包含 15 个不同的信号。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 11,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未指出 DEPT-135 谱图结果有 13 个不同的正信号。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 12,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型给出的 [M+H]⁺ m/z 为 424.2，不在评分标准要求的 421-423 区间内。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 13,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型虽列出数据，但未在文本中对高场和低场区的质子分布特征进行逻辑区分和分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 14,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型通过识别~195-200 ppm 信号，正确分析指出了酮羰基的存在。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 15,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型使用的化学术语、单位符号及分子式书写规范准确。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 16,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型完整覆盖了用户请求的 NMR、DEPT 和 ESI-MS 三类测试数据。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 17,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型提供的机理和硼酸作用是对用户明确提问的回答，不属于无关冗余内容。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 18,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"波谱数据使用了表格和列表格式，排版清晰，可读性好。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 19,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在 1H NMR 部分明确提供了氘代试剂 CDCl₃。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id