t the Bank of Japan's policy changes.\n\n## Bank of Japan (BOJ) Policy Timeline: YCC End and Rate Hikes\n\nBased on my research of official BOJ announcements and financial data sources, here's the information you need:\n\n### 1. **End of Yield Curve Control (YCC)**\n\n**Date:** **March 19, 2024**\n\nOn March 19, 2024, the Bank of Japan announced it was ending its negative interest rate policy and Yield Curve Control (YCC), marking the first rate hike in 17 years. This was a historic shift from the long-standing ultra-loose monetary policy.\n\n**Source:** BOJ \"Statement on Monetary Policy\" and \"Changes in the Monetary Policy Framework\" released March 19, 2024\n- BOJ Release: https://www.boj.or.jp/en/mopo/mpmdeci/mpr_2024/k240319a.pdf\n\n### 2. **Rate Hike Episodes Since Ending YCC (Through December 2025)**\n\nHere are all BOJ policy rate hikes from the end of YCC through the expected December 2025 hike:\n\n#### **Hike #1: March 19, 2024**\n- **Rate Change:** From -0.1% to **0.0-0.1%** (effectively ending negative rates)\n- **Announcement Date:** March 19, 2024\n- **Forward Guidance:** BOJ indicated this was the first step in policy normalization while maintaining accommodative conditions\n\n#### **Hike #2: July 31, 2024**\n- **Rate Change:** From 0.0-0.1% to **0.25%**\n- **Announcement Date:** July 31, 2024\n- **Forward Guidance:** BOJ cited rising inflation and wage growth as justification for further normalization\n\n**Source:** BOJ Release: https://www.boj.or.jp/en/mopo/mpmdeci/mpr_2024/k240731a.pdf\n\n#### **Hike #3: October 30, 2025**\n- **Rate Change:** From 0.25% to **0.50%**\n- **Announcement Date:** October 30, 2025\n- **Forward Guidance:** Part of continued policy normalization path\n\n**Source:** BOJ Release (October 30, 2025 \"Statement on Monetary Policy\")\n\n#### **Hike #4 (Expected): December 19, 2025**\n- **Rate Change:** From 0.50% to **0.75%**\n- **Announcement Date:** December 19, 2025 (scheduled)\n- **Status:** This was an expected hike according to Trading Economics calendar and market expectations\n\n**Source:** \n- Trading Economics data shows this hike was expected\n- BOJ Release: December 19, 2025 \"Change in the Guideline for Money Market Operations\"\n\n### 3. **Summary for T-1 and T+7 Calculations**\n\nFor your asset performance analysis, here are the exact announcement dates:\n\n| Hike # | Announcement Date | Previous Rate | New Rate | Days Since YCC End |\n|--------|------------------|---------------|----------|-------------------|\n| 1 | **March 19, 2024** | -0.1% | 0.0-0.1% | 0 (YCC end date) |\n| 2 | **July 31, 2024** | 0.0-0.1% | 0.25% | 134 days |\n| 3 | **October 30, 2025** | 0.25% | 0.50% | 590 days |\n| 4 | **December 19, 2025** | 0.50% | 0.75% | 640 days |\n\n### Key Notes:\n\n1. **YCC End Date Confirmation:** The March 19, 2024 announcement explicitly ended both negative interest rates and YCC framework in the same decision.\n\n2. **Forward Guidance Common Themes:** Across all hikes, the BOJ emphasized:\n   - Gradual policy normalization\n   - Data-dependent approach (focusing on wage growth and inflation)\n   - Maintaining accommodative financial conditions\n   - Avoiding abrupt changes that could disrupt markets\n\n3. **Current Rate (as of March 2026):** The BOJ maintained the rate at 0.75% at its January 2026 meeting, which remains the highest level since September 1995.\n\n4. **Market Context:** The March 2024 hike was particularly significant as it was the first rate increase since 2007 (17 years), marking a major shift away from decades of ultra-loose policy.\n\n### Sources Used:\n- Bank of Japan Official Website: Monetary Policy Releases 2024-2025\n- Trading Economics: Japan Interest Rate data\n- BOJ Statements on Monetary Policy for March 19, 2024, July 31, 2024, October 30, 2025, and December 19, 2025\n\nThis timeline should provide you with precise dates for calculating T-1 (prior trading day close) and T+7 (7th calendar day after announcement, excluding announcement day) performance windows for your asset performance analysis during BOJ tightening cycles.", "title": "Task ctx_mmu9hzjv00003GG1", "metadata": {"taskId": "ctx_mmu9hzjv00003GG1", "status": "completed", "found": true, "description": "Research BOJ YCC and rate hikes", "timeout": 90, "truncated": false}, "time": {"start": 1773730765214, "end": 1773730853289}}}, {"id": "prt_cfa98f1aa001tSbph2YseBUEcc", "sessionID": "ses_305690a9dffeaAOJ6rrRX0Zsbu", "messageID": "msg_cfa978f7b002ID8y3S49rJydEM", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904", "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 27736, "output": 95, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}}]}, {"id": "msg_cfa98ea2a001Yqhwgu4O4u7Pq7", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa98ea2a001Yqhwgu4O4u7Pq7", "sessionID": "ses_305690a9dffeaAOJ6rrRX0Zsbu", "role": "user", "time": {"created": 1773730851370}, "summary": {"title": "1 tasks done — back to work", "diffs": [{"file": "fetch_market_data.py", "before": "", "after": "#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nFetch equity index performance data for BOJ rate hike analysis\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport datetime\nfrom urllib.request import urlopen\nfrom urllib.error import HTTPError\nimport time\n\n# BOJ rate hike announcement dates\nHIKE_DATES = [\"2024-03-19\", \"2024-07-31\", \"2025-10-30\", \"2025-12-19\"]\n\n# Index symbols for Yahoo Finance\nINDICES = {\n    \"Shanghai Composite\": \"^SSEC\",\n    \"Dow Jones\": \"^DJI\",\n    \"Nasdaq Composite\": \"^IXIC\",\n    \"Nikkei 225\": \"^N225\",\n}\n\n\ndef get_t_minus_1_and_t_plus_7(announcement_date_str):\n    \"\"\"Calculate T-1 and T+7 dates for a given announcement date\"\"\"\n    ann_date = datetime.datetime.strptime(announcement_date_str, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n\n    # T-1: Previous trading day (subtract 1-3 days to ensure we get a trading day)\n    t_minus_1 = ann_date - datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    # If it's Sunday (6) or Monday (0), adjust to get Friday\n    if t_minus_1.weekday() == 6:  # Sunday\n        t_minus_1 = ann_date - datetime.timedelta(days=2)\n    elif t_minus_1.weekday() == 0:  # Monday\n        t_minus_1 = ann_date - datetime.timedelta(days=3)\n\n    # T+7: 7 calendar days after announcement (excluding announcement day)\n    t_plus_7 = ann_date + datetime.timedelta(\n        days=8\n    )  # +7 days after, +1 to exclude announcement day\n\n    # Ensure T+7 is a trading day (Mon-Fri)\n    if t_plus_7.weekday() == 5:  # Saturday\n        t_plus_7 += datetime.timedelta(days=2)\n    elif t_plus_7.weekday() == 6:  # Sunday\n        t_plus_7 += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n\n    return t_minus_1.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\"), t_plus_7.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n\n\ndef fetch_yahoo_data(symbol, start_date, end_date):\n    \"\"\"Attempt to fetch data from Yahoo Finance\"\"\"\n    # Convert dates to timestamps\n    start_ts = int(datetime.datetime.strptime(start_date, \"%Y-%m-%d\").timestamp())\n    end_ts = int(datetime.datetime.strptime(end_date, \"%Y-%m-%d\").timestamp())\n\n    url = f\"https://query1.finance.yahoo.com/v7/finance/download/{symbol}?period1={start_ts}&period2={end_ts}&interval=1d&events=history\"\n\n    print(f\"Fetching {symbol} from {start_date} to {end_date}...\")\n\n    try:\n        with urlopen(url) as response:\n            data = response.read().decode(\"utf-8\")\n            return data\n    except HTTPError as e:\n        print(f\"Error fetching {symbol}: {e}\")\n        return None\n\n\ndef parse_csv_data(csv_data, target_date):\n    \"\"\"Extract closing price for a specific date from CSV data\"\"\"\n    if not csv_data:\n        return None\n\n    lines = csv_data.strip().split(\"\\n\")\n    # Skip header\n    for line in lines[1:]:\n        cols = line.split(\",\")\n        if cols[0] == target_date:\n            return float(cols[4])  # Close price\n\n    return None\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"BOJ Rate Hike Equity Index Performance Analysis\")\n    print(\"=\" * 70)\n\n    results = {}\n\n    for hike_date in HIKE_DATES:\n        results[hike_date] = {}\n        t_minus_1, t_plus_7 = get_t_minus_1_and_t_plus_7(hike_date)\n\n        print(f\"\\nHike Date: {hike_date}\")\n        print(f\"T-1 Date: {t_minus_1}\")\n        print(f\"T+7 Date: {t_plus_7}\")\n        print(\"-\" * 50)\n\n        for index_name, symbol in INDICES.items():\n            print(f\"\\nProcessing {index_name} ({symbol})...\")\n\n            # Fetch T-1 data (fetch range around that date)\n            t1_start = (\n                datetime.datetime.strptime(t_minus_1, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n                - datetime.timedelta(days=5)\n            ).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n            t1_end = (\n                datetime.datetime.strptime(t_minus_1, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n                + datetime.timedelta(days=2)\n            ).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n\n            # Fetch T+7 data\n            t7_start = (\n                datetime.datetime.strptime(t_plus_7, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n                - datetime.timedelta(days=2)\n            ).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n            t7_end = (\n                datetime.datetime.strptime(t_plus_7, \"%Y-%m-%d\")\n                + datetime.timedelta(days=2)\n            ).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d\")\n\n            # Get T-1 closing price\n            time.sleep(1)  # Rate limiting\n            t1_data = fetch_yahoo_data(symbol, t1_start, t1_end)\n            t1_close = parse_csv_data(t1_data, t_minus_1)\n\n            # Get T+7 closing price\n            time.sleep(1)  # Rate limiting\n            t7_data = fetch_yahoo_data(symbol, t7_start, t7_end)\n            t7_close = parse_csv_data(t7_data, t_plus_7)\n\n            # Calculate return\n            if t1_close and t7_close:\n                return_pct = ((t7_close - t1_close) / t1_close) * 100\n                results[hike_date][index_name] = {\n                    \"T-1_Date\": t_minus_1,\n                    \"T-1_Close\": round(t1_close, 2),\n                    \"T+7_Date\": t_plus_7,\n                    \"T+7_Close\": round(t7_close, 2),\n                    \"Return_%\": round(return_pct, 2),\n                }\n                print(\n                    f\"  ✓ T-1: {t1_close:.2f}, T+7: {t7_close:.2f}, Return: {return_pct:.2f}%\"\n                )\n            else:\n                results[hike_date][index_name] = {\n                    \"T-1_Date\": t_minus_1,\n                    \"T-1_Close\": \"N/A\",\n                    \"T+7_Date\": t_plus_7,\n                    \"T+7_Close\": \"N/A\",\n                    \"Return_%\": \"N/A\",\n                }\n                print(f\"  ✗ Data not available\")\n\n    # Save results\n    with open(\"boj_hike_results.json\", \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(results, f, indent=2)\n\n    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n    print(\"Results saved to boj_hike_results.json\")\n\n    # Print formatted table\n    print(\"\\nFORMATTED RESULTS TABLE:\")\n    print(\"=\" * 100)\n    for hike_date, data in results.items():\n        print(f\"\\nHike Date: {hike_date}\")\n        print(\"-\" * 100)\n        print(\n            f\"{'Index':<25} {'T-1 Date':<12} {'T-1 Close':<12} {'T+7 Date':<12} {'T+7 Close':<12} {'Return %':<10}\"\n        )\n        print(\"-\" * 100)\n        for index_name, values in data.items():\n            print(\n                f\"{index_name:<25} {values['T-1_Date']:<12} {values['T-1_Close']:<12} {values['T+7_Date']:<12} {values['T+7_Close']:<12} {values['Return_%']:<10}\"\n            )\n        print()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n", "additions": 180, "deletions": 0}]}, "agent": "synergy", "model": {"providerID": "sii-holos", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B"}}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa98ea2a002AgS8M4XKrEn2IG", "sessionID": "ses_305690a9dffeaAOJ6rrRX0Zsbu", "messageID": "msg_cfa98ea2a001Yqhwgu4O4u7Pq7", "type": "text", "text": "<system-reminder>\n[ALL BACKGROUND TASKS COMPLETE]\n\n**Completed:**\n- `ctx_mmu9hzjv00003GG1`: Research BOJ YCC and rate hikes (completed, 1m 28s)\n\n**DAG update:** 1 node(s) are now running with all dependencies met: `research-boj-history` (scout)\nConsider dispatching them via `task(background=true, dag_node_id=\"<id>\")` for parallel execution.\n\nUse `task_output(task_id=\"<id>\")` to retrieve each result.\nContinue with your work - results are ready.\n</system-reminder>", "synthetic": true}]}, {"id": "msg_cfa98f1dc001rJpR33nrkhVFyI", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa98f1dc001rJpR33nrkhVFyI", "sessionID": "ses_305690a9dffeaAOJ6rrRX0Zsbu", "role": "assistant", "time": {"created": 1773730853340, "completed": 1773730894486}, "parentID": "msg_cfa98ea2a001Yqhwgu4O4u7Pq7", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B", "providerID": "sii-holos", "mode": "synergy", "agent": "synergy", "path": {"cwd": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/economics_and_finance__2816__global/omb-batch", "root": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/economics_and_finance__2816__global/omb-batch"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 29131, "output": 458, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "finish": "tool-calls"}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa98fe020017W92WBsIf8qvlE", "sessionID": "ses_305690a9dffeaAOJ6rrRX0Zsbu", "messageID": "msg_cfa98f1dc001rJpR33nrkhVFyI", "type": "step-start", "snapshot": "4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904"}, {"id": "prt_cfa98fe03001GnD4eQliNEQSzl", "sessionID": "ses_305690a9dffeaAOJ6rrRX0Zsbu", "messageID": "msg_cfa98f1dc001rJpR33nrkhVFyI", "type": "reasoning", "text": "Good, I have the BOJ rate hike dates. Now I need to gather asset performance data for each episode. Let me update the DAG and dispatch multiple data gathering tasks in parallel.\n\nThe key dates are:\n1. March 19, 2024 - YCC end, rate from -0.1% to 0.0-0.1%\n2. July 31, 2024 - rate from 0.0-0.1% to 0.25%\n3. October 30, 2025 - rate from 0.25% to 0.50%\n4. December 19, 2025 - rate from 0.50% to 0.75% (expected)\n\nFor T-1 and T+7 calculations:\n1. March 19, 2024: T-1 = March 18, 2024; T+