ardware unit despite overall decline*\n\n### **2. Operating Profit & FX Impact**\n\n**Operating Profit (in ¥100 million units as requested):**\n- **FY2024**: 5,289.4 hundred million yen (528.941 billion yen)\n- **FY2025**: 2,825.5 hundred million yen (282.553 billion yen)\n- **Growth Rate**: -46.6%\n- *Page Reference: Page 1 (Lines 17-46) and Page 7 (Lines 844-848)*\n\n**Foreign Exchange (FX) Information:**\n- **FY2024 Foreign Exchange Gains**: 61,589 million yen (non-operating income)\n- **FY2025 Foreign Exchange Gains**: 0 million yen (no gains reported)\n- **FY2024 Foreign Exchange Losses**: 496 million yen (non-operating expenses)\n- **FY2025 Foreign Exchange Losses**: 8,630 million yen (non-operating expenses)\n- *Net FX Impact: FY2024 had significant gains (61.6B yen), FY2025 had losses (8.6B yen)*\n- *Page Reference: Page 7 (Lines 862-897)*\n\n**Operating Profit Growth Rate Excluding FX Impact:**\nThe net FX impact alone shows a swing of ~70 billion yen (from +61.6B to -8.6B). However, the specific FX component embedded in operating profit is not separately disclosed in these financial statements. The waterfall chart with factors affecting operating profit changes would typically be in the supplementary explanatory materials.\n\n### **3. Digital Revenue**\n\n**Digital Sales:**\n- **FY2025**: 326.0 billion yen (26.5% decrease YoY)\n- **FY2024**: ~443.8 billion yen (calculated from decline)\n- *Page Reference: Page 1, paragraph 2 (Line 429)*\n\n**Digital Sales Proportion to Total Dedicated Video Game Platform Software Revenue:**\n- **Total Net Sales (FY2025)**: 1,164.9 billion yen\n- **Mobile & IP Related Sales**: 67.6 billion yen\n- **Dedicated Video Game Platform Revenue**: ~1,097.3 billion yen\n- **Digital Sales Proportion**: 29.7% (326.0 / 1,097.3)\n- *Note: This represents digital downloads, DLC, and online services as a percentage of total platform revenue*\n\n**Nintendo Switch Online (NSO):**\n- Specific membership numbers are **NOT disclosed** in this financial results document\n- NSO performance is typically mentioned in supplementary materials or earnings presentations\n\n**Add-on Content:**\n- Specific growth figures not disclosed in this document\n\n### **4. R&D and Inventory**\n\n**Research & Development (R&D):**\n- **R&D is included in Selling, General & Administrative (SG&A) Expenses**\n- **FY2024 SG&A**: 425.4 billion yen (4,253.9 in ¥100 million units)\n- **FY2025 SG&A**: 427.6 billion yen (4,276.1 in ¥100 million units)\n- *Note: R&D expenses are not broken out separately from SG&A in these consolidated financial statements*\n- *Page Reference: Page 7 (Lines 838-842)*\n\n**Inventory:**\n- **FY2024 Ending Balance**: 155.99 billion yen (1,559.9 in ¥100 million units)\n- **FY2025 Ending Balance**: 486.43 billion yen (4,864.3 in ¥100 million units)\n- **Change**: +211.8% increase\n- *Page Reference: Page 5, Balance Sheet (Lines 545-549)*\n\n**Inventory Turnover Days (calculated):**\n- **Raw materials and inventories as of FY2025**: 486.4 billion yen\n- **Inventory Turnover Days (FY2025)**: ~258 days\n- *Formula: (Average Inventory / Cost of Sales) × 365 = ((155.99+486.43)/2 / 454.75) × 365*\n- *This represents a significant increase from the previous year, likely due to preparations for Nintendo Switch 2 launch*\n\n---\n\n## **Summary of Key Insights:**\n\n1. **Declining Switch Hardware Sales**: Hardware sales declined 31.2% to 10.80M units (FY2025), showing the platform's maturity in its 9th year.\n\n2. **Improved Software Attach Rate**: Despite lower absolute numbers, attach rate improved from 12.73 to 14.39, indicating stronger engagement among remaining users.\n\n3. **Significant Operating Profit Decline**: Operating profit dropped 46.6%, partly due to the absence of large FY2024 titles (Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom, Super Mario Bros. Wonder).\n\n4. **Inventory Build-Up**: Inventory increased by 212% to 486.4B yen, likely in preparation for the Nintendo Switch 2 launch (June 5, 2025).\n\n5. **Digital Transition**: Digital sales represent 29.7% of platform revenue, showing continued growth in digital distribution despite a 26.5% decline in FY2025.\n\n6. **No Separate R&D Disclosure**: R&D expenses are combined with SG&A and not separately disclosed in this document.\n\n---\n\n## **Missing Data Points:**\n\n- **Specific FX Impact from Waterfall Chart**: The promised explanatory material with waterfall charts would show the specific FX impact on operating profit changes\n- **NSO Membership Numbers**: Not disclosed in this document\n- **Detailed R&D Expenses**: Not broken out from SG&A\n- **Raw Material Breakdown**: Inventory balance includes finished goods, work-in-progress, and raw materials but detailed breakdown not provided\n\nThe documents retrieved are the main Consolidated Financial Highlights (PDF 1), a Dividend Notice (PDF 2), and Personnel Changes (PDF 3). More detailed data would typically be found in the full earnings presentation materials which were referenced but not included in these particular PDFs.", "title": "Task ctx_mmu9nogo00008mM8", "metadata": {"taskId": "ctx_mmu9nogo00008mM8", "status": "completed", "found": true, "description": "Extract FY2025 Nintendo financial data", "timeout": 120, "truncated": false}, "time": {"start": 1773731096293, "end": 1773731158355}}}, {"id": "prt_cfa9d9954001oVQT06rXH3yUIz", "sessionID": "ses_305675438ffecYfB3l74idZvhs", "messageID": "msg_cfa9c52400029d2ycgm0s0ODLL", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "3159cb0677563d3a6930373dcffd74f6e3974337", "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 129237, "output": 91, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}}, {"id": "prt_cfa9d995a001KrzEBl324QYoK3", "sessionID": "ses_305675438ffecYfB3l74idZvhs", "messageID": "msg_cfa9c52400029d2ycgm0s0ODLL", "type": "patch", "hash": "84180f0c3be1d0b5f7b817af6e52da013b0da19c", "files": ["/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/economics_and_finance__7727__global/