bV", "type": "text", "text": "\n\nThe PDFs are encrypted. Based on the comprehensive data extracted by the scout agent from the FY2025 financial results, let me now compile the complete de-noised analysis you requested. I have sufficient data from the scout's extraction to provide the analysis:\n\n---\n\n# **Nintendo FY2025 De-noised Financial Analysis**\n## **Isolating Yen Depreciation Impact on Core Business Decline**\n\n---\n\n## **Executive Summary**\n\nNintendo's FY2025 (ending March 31, 2025) financial results reveal a company in transition: the Switch platform is in its terminal phase with hardware sales down **31.2%**, while the software ecosystem shows remarkable resilience with an **attach rate reaching 14.39** (up from 12.73 in FY2024). However, the headline operating profit decline of **46.6%** masks an even steeper contraction when excluding the favorable FX impact from yen depreciation.\n\n**Key Exchange Rates:**\n- FY2024 Average: 144.52 JPY/USD\n- FY2025 Average: 152.48 JPY/USD (+5.5% depreciation)\n- FY2025 Period-end: 149.48 JPY/USD\n\n---\n\n## **1. Hardware Decline and Attach Rate Analysis**\n\n### **Sales Volume Data**\n\n| Metric | FY2024 | FY2025 | YoY Change |\n|--------|--------|--------|------------|\n| **Switch Hardware** | 15.70 million units | 10.80 million units | **-31.2%** |\n| **Switch Software** | 199.7", "time": {"start": 1773731177354}}]}]}, "result": {"answer": "Let me try to access the explanatory materials PDF directly from Nintendo's Japanese IR site:", "case_id": 7727, "language": "global", "tags": {"topics": ["Economics and Finance", "Investing", "Equities"], "time_sensitivity": {"time_sensitivity": "Weakly time-sensitive", "year_month": "NA", "day": "NA"}}, "rubric_count": 18}, "metrics": {"solve_time_seconds": 360.1, "tokens": {"input": 1000982, "output": 2368, "total": 1003350}, "cost": 0.0, "step_count": 16}, "error": "Timed out after 360s"}}
