ses severe mediastinitis if leaked; water-soluble is safer |\n| **Sensitivity** | ~80-90% for detecting anastomotic leak |\n\n**If Esophagogram Inconclusive but High Suspicion:**\n- **CT Chest with Oral Contrast** — can show leak location, extent of contamination, abscess formation\n- **Endoscopy** — Direct visualization BUT risk of enlarging leak; reserved for when intervention planned\n\n---\n\n### **Immediate Management Priorities:**\n\n| Priority | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| **1. Resuscitation** | IV fluids, broad-spectrum antibiotics (cover gram-negative + anaerobes), vasopressors if needed |\n| **2. Source Control** | Chest tube drainage of pleural space; may need additional drains |\n| **3. Nutritional Support** | NPO, start TPN or jejunostomy feeding |\n| **4. Definitive Treatment** | Small contained leak: conservative management; Large leak: surgical revision or endoscopic stent |\n| **5. ICU Admission** | Mandatory for sepsis management |\n\n**Mortality Risk:** Anastomotic leak after esophagectomy carries 10-20% mortality; early recognition and intervention critical.", "case_id": 5259, "language": "global", "tags": {"topics": ["Healthcare and Medicine", "Clinical Medicine", "Cardiothoracic Surgery"], "time_sensitivity": {"time_sensitivity": "Time-agnostic", "year_month": "NA", "day": "NA"}}, "rubric_count": 13}, "metrics": {"solve_time_seconds": 138.6, "tokens": {"input": 26582, "output": 3135, "total": 29717}, "cost": 0.0, "step_count": 1}, "error": ""}}
{"task_id": "healthcare_and_medicine/8473/global", "answer": "Based on my medical knowledge and the clinical information provided, let me provide a comprehensive treatment plan for this patient:\n\n## **Clinical Summary**\n\nThis is a patient with:\n- **Underlying etiology**: Chronic Hepatitis B (20 years, untreated)\n- **Diagnosis**: Advanced hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC)\n- **Prior treatments**: \n  - Lenvatinib (10 months)\n  - TACE × 8 sessions\n  - Currently on Regorafenib\n- **Current status**: Disease progression with viable tumor residue\n- **AFP**: Markedly elevated at 1,920 ng/mL\n\n---\n\n## **Treatment Recommendations**\n\n### **1. Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor Therapy (PRIORITY RECOMMENDATION)**\n\nGiven the progression on both TKI therapy (lenvatinib → regorafenib) and locoregional therapy (TACE × 8), **immunotherapy should be strongly considered**:\n\n**Option A: Nivolumab + Ipilimumab Combination**\n- **Rationale**: The CheckMate 040 trial demonstrated objective response rates of 33% in TKI-pretreated HCC patients\n- **Dosing**: Nivolumab 1 mg/kg + Ipilimumab 3 mg/kg every 3 weeks for 4 doses, then nivolumab 240-480 mg every 2-4 weeks\n- **Advantage**: Durable responses in a subset of patients, particularly relevant given the high AFP suggesting aggressive biology\n\n**Option B: Pembrolizumab Monotherapy**\n- **Rationale**: KEYNOTE-240 showed survival benefit in second-line setting after sorafenib\n- **Consider if**: Combination immunotherapy contraindicated or unavailable\n\n**Option C: Atezolizumab + Bevacizumab** (if not previously contraindicated)\n- **Note**: Typically first-line, but could be considered if no prior exposure\n- **Caution**: Must assess for varices/bleeding risk before bevacizumab\n\n### **2. Continue/Modify Anti-Angiogenic Therapy**\n\n**Current Regorafenib Assessment:**\n- If patient is tolerating regorafenib without significant toxicity, **consider continuing** while adding immunotherapy\n- If progression is clear on regorafenib alone, **discontinue** and transition to immunotherapy-based regimen\n\n### **3. Hepatitis B Management (CRITICAL)**\n\n**Immediate Action Required:**\n- **Start/optimise antiviral therapy**: Entecavir 0.5 mg daily OR Tenofovir 300 mg daily\n- **Rationale**: \n  - Immunotherapy can cause HBV reactivation\n  - Antiviral therapy may improve HCC outcomes\n  - Essential before any immunosuppressive or immune-modulating treatment\n- **Monitor**: HBV DNA levels, liver function tests\n\n### **4. Locoregional Therapy Considerations**\n\n**For the residual viable tumor at hepatic dome:**\n- **SBRT (Stereotactic Body Radiation Therapy)**: Consider for the enhancing residual lesion if technically feasible\n- **Repeat TACE**: Given 8 prior sessions with diminishing returns, likely limited benefit\n- **Radioembolization (Y-90)**: Could be considered if liver function permits and anatomy is suitable\n\n### **5. Clinical Trial Enrollment (STRONGLY RECOMMENDED)**\n\nGiven the refractory nature of this disease, clinical trials should be prioritized:\n\n**Types of trials to seek:**\n- Novel immunotherapy combinations\n- HCC-specific CAR-T cell therapies\n- New targeted agents (FGF19/FGFR4 inhibitors, MET inhibitors)\n- Combination of immunotherapy with locoregional therapy\n\n### **6. Supportive Care Measures**\n\n- **AFP monitoring**: Every 4-6 weeks to assess treatment response\n- **Imaging surveillance**: MRI or CT every 8-12 weeks per RECIST/mRECIST criteria\n- **Liver function monitoring**: Child-Pugh score, bilirubin, albumin, INR\n- **Performance status assessment**: ECOG status to guide treatment tolerance\n- **Nutritional support**: Given the chronic disease burden\n- **Pain management**: For abdominal pain symptoms\n\n### **7. Gallbladder Fossa Lesion**\n\n- **Further evaluation needed**: The lesion connected to cystic duct requires clarification\n- **Consider**: MRCP or ERCP to evaluate biliary anatomy\n- **Rule out**: Direct tumor invasion vs. secondary cholelithiasis\n- **Management**: May require surgical consultation if causing obstruction\n\n---\n\n## **Proposed Treatment Sequence**\n\n```\nWeek 0-2:\n├── Start HBV antiviral therapy (Entecavir/Tenofovir)\n├── Baseline assessment: LFTs, HBV DNA, ECOG status, Child-Pugh score\n└── Clinical trial screening\n\nWeek 2-4:\n├── If trial available → Enroll\n├── If no trial → Initiate Nivolumab + Ipilimumab\n└── Discontinue regorafenib if clear progression\n\nWeek 6-12:\n├── First response assessment (imaging + AFP)\n├── Consider SBRT for residual dome lesion if oligoprogressive\n└── Continue immunotherapy if responding/stable\n\nOngoing:\n├── AFP every 4-6 weeks\n├── Imaging every 8-12 weeks\n└── Supportive care optimization\n```\n\n---\n\n## **Prognostic Considerations**\n\n**Favorable factors:**\n- Prior treatment response (10 months on lenvatinib suggests some sensitivity)\n- Post-treatment changes showing mostly non-enhancing tumor (treatment effect)\n\n**Unfavorable factors:**\n- Very high AFP (>1000 ng/mL associated with poorer prognosis)\n- Multiple treatment failures\n- Large tumor burden\n- Long-standing untreated HBV\n\n**Expected outcomes with immunotherapy:**\n- Objective response rate: 15-33% in third-line setting\n- Disease control rate: 40-60%\n- Median overall survival: 8-15 months (highly variable based on response)\n\n---\n\n## **Key Recommendations Summary**\n\n1. **Initiate HBV antiviral therapy immediately** (critical safety issue)\n2. **Transition to immunotherapy** (nivolumab + ipilimumab preferred)\n3. **Strongly pursue clinical trial enrollment**\n4. **Consider SBRT for oligoprogressive residual disease**\n5. **Discontinue regorafenib** if clear progression documented\n6. **Evaluate gallbladder fossa lesion** with MRCP/ERCP\n7. **Close monitoring** with AFP and imaging\n\n---\n\n**Important Note**: This treatment plan should be discussed with a multidisciplinary tumor board including hepatology, medical oncology, interventional radiology, and radiation oncology. Treatment decisions must account for liver function reserve (Child-Pugh class), performance status, comorbidities, and patient preferences.", "score": {"rubric_results": [{"rubric_number": 1, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型未建议进行全身 PET-CT 或涵盖胸腹盆的增强 CT 以完成全面分期评估，仅提及了随访时的影像监测。"}, {"rubric_number": 2, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型在支持性护理措施和基线评估中明确列出了 Child-Pugh 评分作为肝功能储备评估指标。"}, {"rubric_number": 3, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型在支持性护理措施和基线评估中明确提到了使用 ECOG 评分评估患者体能状态。"}, {"rubric_number": 4, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型在临床总结中明确指出当前状态为疾病进展，并基于 AFP 升高和影像残留建议若进展明确则停用瑞戈非尼。"}, {"rubric_number": 5, "weight": 7, "met": true, "reason": "模型核心建议调整为免疫治疗（如纳武利尤单抗 + 伊匹木单抗），属于 TKI 治疗后的序贯治疗策略。"}, {"rubric_number": 6, "weight": -5, "met": true, "reason": "模型未明确陈述 Child-Pugh C 级患者通常不推荐使用免疫疗法这一禁忌症，符合扣分项描述。"}, {"rubric_number": 7, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型在局部治疗考虑中明确建议对肝圆顶残留病灶考虑立体定向放射治疗（SBRT）。"}, {"rubric_number": 8, "weight": 7, "met": true, "reason": "模型在乙肝管理部分明确列出了恩替卡韦和替诺福韦作为具体的抗病毒药物。"}, {"rubric_number": 9, "weight": 4, "met": false, "reason": "模型提及了免疫治疗引起乙肝复发的风险，但未明确阐述病毒活动加速肝损伤和肝癌进展这一具体机制。"}, {"rubric_number": 10, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型建议影像学监测每 8-12 周（即 2-3 个月）一次，符合随访频率要求，AFP 监测频率更为频繁。"}, {"rubric_number": 11, "weight": -10, "met": true, "reason": "模型全文未提及肝移植作为肿瘤控制后的后续考虑选项，符合扣分项描述。"}, {"rubric_number": 12, "weight": -7, "met": true, "reason": "模型未提及米兰标准或 UCSF 标准作为评估肝移植可行性的参考，符合扣分项描述。"}, {"rubric_number": 13, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型回复结构缺少后续的肝移植评估部分，未完全符合评分标准要求的三个主要章节结构。"}, {"rubric_number": 14, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型逻辑链完整，从基线评估（肝功能、体能）开始，到具体的免疫联合或局部治疗方案，层次清晰。"}, {"rubric_number": 15, "weight": -4, "met": false, "reason": "模型开头以结构化摘要形式呈现病史，未出现机械性冗长复述导致严重冗余的情况。"}, {"rubric_number": 16, "weight": -5, "met": false, "reason": "模型使用了标题、列表和代码块等格式，未出现大段密集纯文本，阅读体验良好。"}, {"rubric_number": 17, "weight": -5, "met": false, "reason": "模型包含了营养支持和考虑患者偏好等内容，未完全缺失人文关怀和生活方式建议。"}], "score": 18, "max_score": 54, "raw_response": "[\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未建议进行全身 PET-CT 或涵盖胸腹盆的增强 CT 以完成全面分期评估，仅提及了随访时的影像监测。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 2,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在支持性护理措施和基线评估中明确列出了 Child-Pugh 评分作为肝功能储备评估指标。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 3,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在支持性护理措施和基线评估中明确提到了使用 ECOG 评分评估患者体能状态。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 4,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在临床总结中明确指出当前状态为疾病进展，并基于 AFP 升高和影像残留建议若进展明确则停用瑞戈非尼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 5,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型核心建议调整为免疫治疗（如纳武利尤单抗 + 伊匹木单抗），属于 TKI 治疗后的序贯治疗策略。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 6,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未明确陈述 Child-Pugh C 级患者通常不推荐使用免疫疗法这一禁忌症，符合扣分项描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 7,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在局部治疗考虑中明确建议对肝圆顶残留病灶考虑立体定向放射治疗（SBRT）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 8,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在乙肝管理部分明确列出了恩替卡韦和替诺福韦作为具体的抗病毒药物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 9,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型提及了免疫治疗引起乙肝复发的风险，但未明确阐述病毒活动加速肝损伤和肝癌进展这一具体机制。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 10,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型建议影像学监测每 8-12 周（即 2-3 个月）一次，符合随访频率要求，AFP 监测频率更为频繁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 11,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型全文未提及肝移植作为肿瘤控制后的后续考虑选项，符合扣分项描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 12,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未提及米兰标准或 UCSF 标准作为评估肝移植可行性的参考，符合扣分项描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 13,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型回复结构缺少后续的肝移植评估部分，未完全符合评分标准要求的三个主要章节结构。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 14,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型逻辑链完整，从基线评估（肝功能、体能）开始，到具体的免疫联合或局部治疗方案，层次清晰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 15,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型开头以结构化摘要形式呈现病史，未出现机械性冗长复述导致严重冗余的情况。\"\n  },\n  {\