 Limited details on specific FX intervention amounts, capital control measures\n\n5. **Hedging Instrument Liquidity**: NDF market depth and pricing not transparent\n\n6. **VND Forecasts**: Available but widely varying (Trading Economics vs. other forecasters)\n\n---\n\n## ALTERNATIVE DATA SOURCES NEEDED\n\nFor complete analysis, you would need:\n\n1. **Bloomberg Terminal**:\n   - Vietnam Sovereign CDS curves\n   - VND NDF liquidity indicators (bid-ask spreads, daily volumes)\n   - Bond maturity schedule\n\n2. **Commercial Real Estate Services**:\n   - CBRE Vietnam Industrial MarketView report\n   - JLL Vietnam Industrial research\n   - Cushman & Wakefield market data\n\n3. **Official Sources**:\n   - State Bank of Vietnam monetary policy statements\n   - Vietnam Ministry of Finance bond issuance calendar\n   - IMF Article IV consultation reports for Vietnam\n\n4. **Financial News Services**:\n   - Reuters detailed coverage of Vietnam real estate sector\n   - Bloomberg Vietnam economy and property news\n\n---\n\n## RECOMMENDATIONS FOR FURTHER RESEARCH\n\n1. **Subscribe** to commercial real estate data services (CBRE, JLL) for industrial park statistics\n\n2. **Access** Bloomberg Terminal for:\n   - VND NDF pricing and liquidity\n   - Vietnam sovereign CDS spreads\n   - Bond market depth and foreign ownership\n\n3. **Review** SBV annual reports and monetary policy statements for:\n   - FX intervention amounts\n   - Capital flow measures\n   - Policy rate rationale\n\n4. **Monitor** Vietnam Ministry of Finance website for:\n   - Government bond issuance schedule\n   - Debt maturity profile\n   - Foreign vs. domestic debt composition\n\n**Sources**:\n- Trading Economics (tradingeconomics.com/vietnam)\n- World Government Bonds (worldgovernmentbonds.com)\n- ExchangeRate-API (api.exchangerate-api.com)\n- Data retrieved March 17, 2026\n\n**Note**: All data is subject to verification through primary sources. Publicly available data has significant gaps for comprehensive hedg