trucking dependency (90%+ freight)\n\n2. **Power Supply Gap Impact**\n   - Northern Vietnam summer shortfall: 2,000-3,000 MW deficit during peak hours\n   - Production loss estimate: 7% output loss in Q2 for electronics manufacturers\n   - Dollar impact: Northern industrial zones generate ~$80-100B annually → 7% loss = $5.6-7B quarterly impact\n   - Backup power costs: Diesel generators add $0.03-0.05/kWh\n\n3. **Low DVA Structure Vulnerability**\n   - Vietnam DVA: 15-25% vs. China 60-70%, Malaysia 40-50%\n   - Import dependency: 95%+ ICs, 90%+ displays, 80%+ PCBs\n   - Value capture: Only 5-8% assembly margin vs. 60-70% upstream component value\n   - FX exposure: High import content amplifies VND depreciation impact on input costs\n\n4. **Combined Margin Squeeze Quantification**\n   - Assembly margins compressed from 8-10% to 5-7%\n   - Total landed cost increased 12-18% (2021-2024)\n   - Company examples: Foxconn 2-3pp margin compression, Samsung 10% operational cost increase\n   - BMI/Fitch assessment: Infrastructure bottlenecks erode margins by 2-4 points vs. projections\n\n**Deliverable:** A concise quantitative summary (300-400 words) with specific numbers, suitable for inclusion in an investment research report. Include a \"Key Risk Metrics\" bullet summary.", "subagent_type": "master"}, "output": "Background task launched.\n\nTask ID: ctx_mmu9w25i000l5vb1\nSession ID: ses_3055e6c19ffeyoKDuVuiHJ5lqU\nDescription: Synthesize margin squeeze analysis\nAgent: master\nStatus: running\n\nYou will be notified when the task completes.\nUse `task_output(task_id=\"ctx_mmu9w25i000l5vb1\")` to check progress or retrieve results.", "title": "[Background] Synthesize margin squeeze analysis", "metadata": {"taskId": "ctx_mmu9w25i000l5vb1", "sessionId": "ses_3055e6c19ffeyoKDuVuiHJ5lqU", "background": true, "summary": [], "truncated": false}, "time": {"start": 1773731419109, "end": 1773731419111}}}, {"id": "prt_cfaa194610018c4BpP5IIhSA65", "sessionID": "ses_305634d05ffe2YiaZOUkZP0VSn", "messageID": "msg_cfaa0ea8d0014odz9IEsAA4zSh", "type": "tool", "callID": "call_6f4647a9d5814f4ab744499e", "tool": "task", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"background": true, "dag_node_id": "synthesis-trade-status", "description": "Synthesize NME trade analysis", "prompt": "Synthesize an analysis of how the U.S. Non-Market Economy (NME) determination disrupts Vietnam's trade positioning. Use the research findings to produce:\n\n**Output Structure:**\n\n1. **NME Methodology Mechanics**\n   - Explain surrogate country approach: DOC uses comparable market economy (India, Indonesia, Bangladesh, Thailand) input costs instead of Vietnam's actual costs\n   - Why this inflates margins: Surrogate countries have higher labor, land, energy costs than Vietnam\n   - Constructed value calculation: Raw materials + labor + energy + overhead + profit from surrogate data\n\n2. **Anti-Dumping Duty Impact**\n   - Steel cases: CORE steel 3.53%-38.34% AD + 0.12%-199.58% CVD (using Indian surrogate financials)\n   - Aluminum extrusions: 5.05%-33.28% AD (Indonesia/India surrogate for energy costs)\n   - Pattern: NME methodology produces 5-200%+ duty ranges vs. single-digit rates for market economies\n\n3. **Transshipment Tariff Layer**\n   - Section 301 (China): 7.5%-25% base rates on List 1-4A products\n   - Anti-circumvention (Section 781): 25%-50% findings on Chinese steel/aluminum routed through Vietnam\n   - Section 232: Additional 25% steel, 10% aluminum duties\n   - Enforcement: CBP increased scrutiny on Vietnam-origin goods with Chinese input content\n\n4. **Investment Distortion Effects**\n   - Unpredictability: Cannot accurately forecast dumping margins due to surrogate selection discretion\n   - Compliance burden: Extensive documentation required to prove Vietnamese origin\n   - China+1 hedging: Multinationals maintain dual sourcing (Vietnam + China/India/Mexico) rather than full relocation\n   - FDI quality impact: Attracts assembly (low DVA) but discourages upstream component investment\n\n**Deliverable:** A concise analytical summary (350-450 words) explaining the NME distortion mechanism and its practical impact on supply chain relocation decisions. Include specific duty rate examples.", "subagent_type": "master"}, "output": "Background task launched.\n\nTask ID: ctx_mmu9w8tt000mCyni\nSession ID: ses_3055e4a4dffehemKVtyqzMAMsw\nDescription: Synthesize NME trade analysis\nAgent: master\nStatus: running\n\nYou will be notified when the task completes.\nUse `task_output(task_id=\"ctx_mmu9w8tt000mCyni\")` to check progress or retrieve results.", "title": "[Background] Synthesize NME trade analysis", "metadata": {"taskId": "ctx_mmu9w8tt000mCyni", "sessionId": "ses_3055e4a4dffehemKVtyqzMAMsw", "background": true, "summary": [], "truncated": false}, "time": {"start": 1773731427760, "end": 1773731427762}}}, {"id": "prt_cfaa1b63c001RK5sq3t1FA69Lq", "sessionID": "ses_305634d05ffe2YiaZOUkZP0VSn", "messageID": "msg_cfaa0ea8d0014odz9IEsAA4zSh", "type": "tool", "callID": "call_fa66ae75ccc74e5889506fc0", "tool": "task", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"background": true, "dag_node_id": "synthesis-admin-efficacy", "description": "Synthesize admin reform impact", "prompt": "Synthesize an assessment of Vietnam's administrative reform impact on infrastructure investment efficacy. Use the research findings to produce:\n\n**Output Structure:**\n\n1. **July 2025 Provincial Consolidation**\n   - Context: Administrative overhaul aimed at efficiency, anti-corruption, cost reduction\n   - Transitional friction: Merger integration creates temporary approval delays, jurisdictional ambiguity\n   - Business council feedback: AmCham/EuroCham reports on regulatory friction during transition\n\n2. **Public Investment Disbursement Problem**\n   - Chronic under-execution: Typically 60-70% of allocated budget actually disbursed\n   - 2024-2025 pattern: Persistently low disbursement despite infrastructure urgency\n   - Root causes: Approval bottlenecks, land acquisition delays, contractor selection challenges\n\n3. **Anti-Corruption \"Blazing Furnace\" Campaign Effects**\n   - High-profile cases: Infrastructure/construction sector investigations (2023-2025)\n   - Behavioral impact: Official risk aversion - \"analytical paralysis\" where approvals delayed due to fear of later investigation\n   - Trade-off: Necessary governance cleanup vs. short-term investment slowdown\n\n4. **Infrastructure Project Impacts**\n   - North-South Expressway: Delays and cost overruns from approval bottlenecks\n   - Long Thanh International Airport: Timeline slippage from land acquisition and contractor issues\n   - Port expansions: Cat Lai and Cai Mep capacity constraints persist due to investment delays\n   - Power grid: Transmission infrastructure lags generation capacity, contributing to regional shortages\n\n5. **Long-Term Institutional Assessment**\n   - Streamlining potential: Consolidated provinces could reduce duplication, improve coordination\n   - Execution risk: Reform benefits materialize only after transition friction resolves (12-24 month lag)\n   - Investment confidence: Anti-corruption is positive long-term but creates near-term uncertainty\n\n**Deliverable:** A balanced analytical summary (350-450 words) assessing whether administrative reform is a temporary friction or structural constraint on infrastructure investment. Include specific project examples.", "subagent_type": "master"}, "output": "Background task launched.\n\nTask ID: ctx_mmu9wm02000oRuOx\nSession ID: ses_3055e079dffe8Lad8rcgVX8F9s\nDescription: Synthesize admin reform impact\nAgent: master\nStatus: running\n\nYou will be notified when the task completes.\nUse `task_output(task_id=\"ctx_mmu9wm02000oRuOx\")` to check progress or retrieve results.", "title": "[Background] Synthesize admin reform impact", "metadata": {"taskId": "ctx_mmu9wm02000oRuOx", "sessionId": "ses_3055e079dffe8Lad8rcgVX8F9s", "background": true, "summary": [], "truncated": false}, "time": {"start": 1773731444833, "end": 1773731444835}}}, {"id": "prt_cfaa1f909001Of26aJ6uyuutwM", "sessionID": "ses_305634d05ffe2YiaZOUkZP0VSn", "messageID": "msg_cfaa0ea8d0014odz9IEsAA4zSh", "type": "tool", "callID": "call_756a842c3bf84ae184341180", "tool": "task", "state": {"status": "pending", "input": {}, "raw": ""}}]}]}, "result": {"answer": "Let me wait for the final research task to complete.", "case_id": 5426, "language": "global", "tags": {"topics": ["Economics and Finance", "Economics", "Macroeconomics"], "time_sensitivity": {"time_sensitivity": "Weakly time-sensitive", "year_month": "2025-12", "day": "NA"}}, "rubric_count": 22}, "metrics": {"solve_time_seconds": 360.1, "tokens": {"input": 119840, "output": 3548, "total": 123388}, "cost": 0.0, "step_count": 5}, "error": "Timed out after 360s"}}
{"task_id": "natural_science/8075/global", "answer": "# Experimental Protocol: Distinguishing Protein X-Mediated Bypass Activation from Canonical EGFR Ligand Signaling\n\n## Overview\n\nThis protocol is designed to demonstrate that Protein X activates the PI3K–AKT–mTOR pathway through a **bypass mechanism** that is mechanistically distinguishable from canonical EGFR ligand (EGF/TGF-α) signaling. The experimental strategy focuses on four key discriminators:\n\n| Discriminator | Canonical (EGF/TGF-α) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| EGFR binding | Direct | None |\n| EGFR phosphorylation | Tyr1068/1173 ↑ | Minimal/absent |\n| EGFR kinase inhibitor sensitivity | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| EGFR dependency | Required | Dispensable |\n\n---\n\n## Experimental Design\n\n### **Aim 1: Demonstrate Protein X Does Not Directly Bind EGFR**\n\n| Experiment | Key Readout | Expected Outcome (Bypass) |\n|-----------|-------------|--------------------------|\n| **Surface Plasmon Resonance (SPR)** | Binding affinity (KD) | No detectable binding between recombinant Protein X and EGFR extracellular domain |\n| **Co-immunoprecipitation** | EGFR–Protein X complex | No co-IP in GL261 cells or tumor lysates |\n| **Ligand-binding competition assay** | Displacement of ¹²⁵I-EGF | Protein X fails to compete with EGF for EGFR binding |\n| **Cellular thermal shift assay (CETSA)** | EGFR thermal stabilization | Protein X does not stabilize EGFR (unlike EGF) |\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 2: Compare EGFR Activation Status**\n\nCanonical EGFR ligands induce **specific tyrosine autophosphorylation patterns**. Bypass activation should show a distinct signature.\n\n| Experiment | Key Readout | Distinguishing Feature |\n|-----------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **Phospho-EGFR Western blot** | pY1068, pY1173, pY992, pY1045 | EGF: strong phosphorylation; Protein X: minimal/no phosphorylation |\n| **EGFR phospho-tyrosine mass spectrometry** | Comprehensive pY profiling | Different phosphorylation site repertoire |\n| **EGFR dimerization assay (BSFRET/crosslinking)** | Receptor oligomerization | EGF induces dimerization; Protein X may not |\n| **EGFR internalization assay** | Surface EGFR downregulation | EGF causes rapid internalization; Protein X may not |\n\n**Key antibodies to use:**\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y1068) – Grb2 binding site\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y1173) – Shc binding site\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y992) – PLCγ binding site\n- Anti-total EGFR\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 3: Differential Sensitivity to EGFR Pathway Inhibitors**\n\nThis is a **critical discriminator** – bypass activation should be resistant to upstream inhibition.\n\n| Inhibitor Class | Specific Agent | Target | Canonical (EGF) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|----------------|----------------|--------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| **EGFR kinase inhibitor** | Erlotinib/Gefitinib | EGFR kinase domain | **Blocks** pAKT | **No effect** on pAKT |\n| **EGFR neutralizing antibody** | Cetuximab/Panitumumab | EGFR extracellular domain | **Blocks** pAKT | **No effect** on pAKT |\n| **PI3K inhibitor** | LY294002/BKM120 | PI3K catalytic subunit | Blocks pAKT | Blocks pAKT |\n| **AKT inhibitor** | MK-2206 | AKT kinase domain | Blocks pS6 | Blocks pS6 |\n| **mTOR inhibitor** | Rapamycin/Everolimus | mTORC1 | Blocks pS6 | Blocks pS6 |\n\n**Experimental setup:**\n- Treat GL261 cells (± Protein X stimulation or EGF stimulation) with inhibitors\n- Measure: pAKT (S473), pS6 (S235/236), p4EBP1 by Western blot\n- **Key criterion:** Protein X-induced pAKT persists despite EGFR inhibition\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 4: Genetic Dissection of EGFR Dependency**\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Expected Outcome (Bypass) |\n|-----------|----------|--------------------------|\n| **EGFR knockout** | CRISPR/Cas9 in GL261 cells | EGF signaling abolished; Protein X signaling **preserved** |\n| **EGFR knockdown** | shRNA/siRNA | EGF signaling reduced; Protein X signaling **unaffected** |\n| **EGFR rescue** | Re-express wild-type vs kinase-dead EGFR | Protein X signaling independent of EGFR status |\n| **Dominant-negative EGFR** | Express EGFR-CD533 (truncated) | Blocks EGF signaling; **no effect** on Protein X |\n\n**Readouts:** pAKT, pS6, cell proliferation, survival assays\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 5: Identify the True Receptor for Protein X**\n\nSince Protein X activates PI3K–AKT–mTOR without EGFR, it must signal through an **alternative receptor**.\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Purpose |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **Protein X pull-down + MS** | Biotinylated Protein X → streptavidin pulldown → LC-MS/MS | Identify binding partners |\n| **Expression screen** | siRNA library against RTKs/GPCRs | Identify receptor required for Protein X signaling |\n| **Phospho-RTK array** | Compare EGF vs Protein X stimulation | Identify which RTKs are activated by Protein X |\n| **Candidate validation** | Knockout/knockdown of candidate receptors | Confirm requirement for Protein X signaling |\n\n**Candidate receptors to prioritize:**\n- Other ErbB family members (HER2/HER3)\n- MET, AXL, PDGFR (known to activate PI3K–AKT)\n- GPCRs that transactivate PI3K (Gβγ-mediated)\n- Integrins (FAK/Src-mediated PI3K activation)\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 6: Signaling Kinetics and Amplitude Comparison**\n\nCanonical and bypass pathways often show **distinct temporal dynamics**.\n\n| Parameter | Measurement | Distinguishing Value |\n|-----------|-------------|---------------------|\n| **Activation kinetics** | pAKT time course (0, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120 min) | EGF: rapid peak (5–15 min); Protein X: may be slower/sustained |\n| **Signal amplitude** | pAKT dose-response | Different EC50 and Emax |\n| **Signal duration** | pAKT after washout | EGF: rapid decay; Protein X: may persist |\n| **Feedback activation** | pERK, pS6K over time | Different feedback loop engagement |\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 7: Transcriptomic Signature Comparison**\n\nCanonical EGFR signaling and bypass activation may drive **distinct gene expression programs**.\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Readout |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **RNA-seq** | GL261 ± EGF ± Protein X (4–8 hr) | Differentially expressed genes |\n| **GSEA** | Compare pathway enrichment | EGFR signature vs alternative RTK signature |\n| **Immediate early genes** | qPCR for FOS, JUN, EGR1 | Different induction patterns |\n\n**Expected:** Protein X induces a transcriptional program distinct from EGF, reflecting different upstream activators.\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 8: In Vivo Validation in GL261 Orthotopic Model**\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Key Readout |\n|-----------|----------|-------------|\n| **EGFR inhibitor treatment** | Erlotinib in tumor-bearing mice | Tumor growth, survival, pAKT in tumor tissue |\n| **PI3K inhibitor treatment** | BKM120 in tumor-bearing mice | Tumor growth, survival, pAKT in tumor tissue |\n| **Protein X neutralization** | Anti-Protein X antibody | Tumor growth, pAKT reduction |\n| **Combined targeting** | EGFRi + anti-Protein X | Additive/synergistic effect suggests independent pathways |\n| **IHC analysis** | pEGFR, pAKT, pS6 in tumor sections | Spatial correlation of Protein X with pAKT but not pEGFR |\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Discriminators\n\n| Criterion | Canonical (EGF/TGF-α) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|-----------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| **Direct EGFR binding** | ✓ | ✗ |\n| **EGFR phosphorylation** | Strong (Y1068, Y1173) | Minimal/absent |\n| **EGFR kinase inhibitor** | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| **EGFR neutralizing antibody** | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| **PI3K/AKT/mTOR inhibitors** | Sensitive | Sensitive |\n| **EGFR knockout** | Abolishes signaling | Signaling preserved |\n| **Alternative receptor** | Not required | Required (to be identified) |\n| **Signaling kinetics** | Rapid, transient | May differ |\n| **Transcriptional signature** | EGFR-dependent | Distinct |\n\n---\n\n## Critical Controls\n\n1. **Positive control:** EGF stimulation (canonical pathway)\n2. **Negative control:** Vehicle treatment\n3. **Specificity control:** Protein X from α-knockout cells/tissue\n4. **Off-target control:** Use ≥2 inhibitors per target class\n5. **Genetic control:** ≥2 independent sgRNAs/shRNAs per target\n\n---\n\n## Expected Conclusions\n\nIf Protein X mediates bypass activation, the data should show:\n\n1. **No direct EGFR binding** (Aim 1)\n2. **No EGFR phosphorylation** despite strong pAKT (Aim 2)\n3. **Resistance to EGFR inhibitors** but sensitivity to PI3K/AKT/mTOR inhibitors (Aim 3)\n4. **Preserved signaling in EGFR-KO cells** (Aim 4)\n5. **Identification of an alternative receptor** (Aim 5)\n\nThis would establish Protein X as activating PI3K–AKT–mTOR through a **mechanistically distinct bypass pathway**, with implications for therapeutic targeting in glioma.", "score": {"rubric_results": [{"rubric_number": 1, "weight": 8, "met": true, "reason": "模型在 Aim 1、Aim 3、Aim 4 等多处明确提及使用 GL261 细胞进行体外实验。"}, {"rubric_number": 2, "weight": 10, "met": true, "reason": "Aim 6 中明确列出了 pAKT time course (0, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120 min) 的时间点。"}, {"rubric_number": 3, "weight": 8, "met": true, "reason": "Aim 2 中明确列出了 pY1068, pY1173, pY1045 等具体的 EGFR 磷酸化位点。"}, {"rubric_number": 4, "weight": 6, "met": true, "reason": "Aim 2 中提到了 EGFR dimerization assay (BSFRET/crosslinking) 来检测受体寡聚化。"}, {"rubric_number": 5, "weight": 10, "met": false, "reason": "模型提到了 pAKT 和 pS6，但在下游信号检测指标中未提及 pSTAT3。"}, {"rubric_number": 6, "weight": 10, "met": true, "reason": "Aim 4 中明确设计了 CRISPR/Cas9 介导的 EGFR knockout 实验以验证信号依赖性。"}, {"rubric_number": 7, "weight": 6, "met": true, "reason": "Aim 3 中明确列出了 Erlotinib/Gefitinib 等 EGFR 特异性激酶抑制剂。"}, {"rubric_number": 8, "weight": 8, "met": true, "reason": "Aim 5 中提出通过 Phospho-RTK array 检测磷酸化谱来识别 Protein X 的上游受体。"}, {"rubric_number": 9, "weight": -10, "met": false, "reason": "模型使用的是 Orthotopic Model（原位模型），而非 Rubric 描述的皮下移植模型，未命中负向扣分项。"}, {"rubric_number": 10, "weight": 8, "met": false, "reason": "模型仅列出了 4 种处理策略，未包含 Rubric 要求的 7 种具体体内实验分组（如过表达组等）。"}, {"rubric_number": 11, "weight": 7, "met": false, "reason": "体内实验检测指标仅列出 pEGFR, pAKT, pS6，未提及 Ki-67 或 Cleaved Caspase-3。"}, {"rubric_number": 12, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "回复结构紧凑，直接进入实验方案，无过多的背景介绍冗余，未命中负向扣分项。"}, {"rubric_number": 13, "weight": -10, "met": false, "reason": "模型包含了 Aim 8 体内验证实验，并非仅进行体外验证，未命中负向扣分项。"}, {"rubric_number": 14, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型仅检测了 EGFR 磷酸化位点（Grb2 binding site），未明确设计检测 GRB2/SHC 蛋白招募（如 Co-IP）的实验。"}, {"rubric_number": 15, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型未明确阐述无结合但高 pEGFR 属于反式激活而非旁路激活的逻辑区分，仅定义旁路为无 pEGFR。"}, {"rubric_number": 16, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "回复结构清晰，有明确的 Aim 编号和表格，逻辑性强，未命中负向扣分项。"}, {"rubric_number": 17, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型在 Overview 和 Summary 中明确区分了旁路激活下 pAKT 升高但 pEGFR/二聚化不变的特征。"}], "score": 61, "max_score": 97, "raw_response": "[\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在 Aim 1、Aim 3、Aim 4 等多处明确提及使用 GL261 细胞进行体外实验。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 2,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"Aim 6 中明确列出了 pAKT time course (0, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120 min) 的时间点。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 3,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"Aim 2 中明确列出了 pY1068, pY1173, pY1045 等具体的 EGFR 磷酸化位点。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 4,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"Aim 2 中提到了 EGFR dimerization assay (BSFRET/crosslinking) 来检测受体寡聚化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 5,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型提到了 pAKT 和 pS6，但在下游信号检测指标中未提及 pSTAT3。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 6,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"Aim 4 中明确设计了 CRISPR/Cas9 介导的 EGFR knockout 实验以验证信号依赖性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 7,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"Aim 3 中明确列出了 Erlotinib/Gefitinib 等 EGFR 特异性激酶抑制剂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 8,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"Aim 5 中提出通过 Phospho-RTK array 检测磷酸化谱来识别 Protein X 的上游受体。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 9,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型使用的是 Orthotopic Model（原位模型），而非 Rubric 描述的皮下移植模型，未命中负向扣分项。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 10,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型仅列出了 4 种处理策略，未包含 Rubric 要求的 7 种具体体内实验分组（如过表达组等）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 11,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"体内实验检测指标仅列出 pEGFR, pAKT, pS6，未提及 Ki-67 或 Cleaved Caspase-3。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 12,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"回复结构紧凑，直接进入实验方案，无过多的背景介绍冗余，未命中负向扣分项。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 13,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型包含了 Aim 8 体内验证实验，并非仅进行体外验证，未命中负向扣分项。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 14,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型仅检测了 EGFR 磷酸化位点（Grb2 binding site），未明确设计检测 GRB2/SHC 蛋白招募（如 Co-IP）的实验。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 15,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未明确阐述无结合但高 pEGFR 属于反式激活而非旁路激活的逻辑区分，仅定义旁路为无 pEGFR。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 16,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"回复结构清晰，有明确的 Aim 编号和表格，逻辑性强，未命中负向扣分项。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 17,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在 Overview 和 Summary 中明确区分了旁路激活下 pAKT 升高但 pEGFR/二聚化不变的特征。\"\n  }\n]"}, "error": null, "stage": null, "system_prompt": "You are a domain expert capable of delivering professional-grade responses in both English and 中文.\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. **Language**: Detect the question's language and respond entirely in that language. For Chinese, use natural, idiomatic professional Chinese — not translation-style. Never mix languages unless a term has no established translation.\n\n2. **Role**: If the question assigns a role, adopt it fully. If not, infer the appropriate expert identity from the scenario.\n\n3. **Scenario Focus**: Address the specific scenario directly. Do not provide generic domain overviews.\n\n4. **Factual Accuracy**: Use precise technical terminology, causal mechanisms, and quantitative specifics. Distinguish consensus from speculation.\n\n5. **Analytical Depth**: Decompose problems logically. Compare options with explicit dimensions and trade-offs. Explain \"why\" and \"how,\" not just \"what.\" Consider edge cases and real-world constraints.\n\n6. **Structure**: Use clear headings, numbered lists for sequences, bullets for parallel items, tables for multi-item comparisons. Lead with the key answer, then elaborate. End longer responses with a summary.\n\n7. **Instruction Following**: Address ALL sub-questions explicitly. Honor any specified constraints exactly.\n\n8. **Prohibitions**: Never fabricate data or citations. Never ignore parts of the question. Never be unnecessarily verbose. Never respond in the wrong language.", "user_prompt": "In a C57BL/6 syngeneic (GL261 cells) orthotopic intracranial glioma model (30 days post-tumor establishment), a specific ligand-like molecule was significantly increased in the tumor group: the expression of gene α was upregulated, and its encoded product, Protein X, was also found at significantly elevated levels in the tumor tissue/tumor microenvironment. Preliminary results suggest that Protein X does not directly bind to EGFR but may activate the canonical downstream PI3K–AKT–mTOR pathway of EGFR via a bypass activation mechanism. Design a detailed experimental protocol (complete experimental procedures are not required, but key experiments and/or indicators must be mentioned) to demonstrate that the bypass activation mediated by Protein X is distinguishable from the canonical pathway triggered by the binding of canonical EGFR ligands (such as EGF/TGF-α) to EGFR.", "response": {"request_id": "omb-batch", "status": "completed", "session_id": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "workspace": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8075__global/omb-batch", "system_prompt": "You are a domain expert capable of delivering professional-grade responses in both English and 中文.\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. **Language**: Detect the question's language and respond entirely in that language. For Chinese, use natural, idiomatic professional Chinese — not translation-style. Never mix languages unless a term has no established translation.\n\n2. **Role**: If the question assigns a role, adopt it fully. If not, infer the appropriate expert identity from the scenario.\n\n3. **Scenario Focus**: Address the specific scenario directly. Do not provide generic domain overviews.\n\n4. **Factual Accuracy**: Use precise technical terminology, causal mechanisms, and quantitative specifics. Distinguish consensus from speculation.\n\n5. **Analytical Depth**: Decompose problems logically. Compare options with explicit dimensions and trade-offs. Explain \"why\" and \"how,\" not just \"what.\" Consider edge cases and real-world constraints.\n\n6. **Structure**: Use clear headings, numbered lists for sequences, bullets for parallel items, tables for multi-item comparisons. Lead with the key answer, then elaborate. End longer responses with a summary.\n\n7. **Instruction Following**: Address ALL sub-questions explicitly. Honor any specified constraints exactly.\n\n8. **Prohibitions**: Never fabricate data or citations. Never ignore parts of the question. Never be unnecessarily verbose. Never respond in the wrong language.", "final_prompt": "In a C57BL/6 syngeneic (GL261 cells) orthotopic intracranial glioma model (30 days post-tumor establishment), a specific ligand-like molecule was significantly increased in the tumor group: the expression of gene α was upregulated, and its encoded product, Protein X, was also found at significantly elevated levels in the tumor tissue/tumor microenvironment. Preliminary results suggest that Protein X does not directly bind to EGFR but may activate the canonical downstream PI3K–AKT–mTOR pathway of EGFR via a bypass activation mechanism. Design a detailed experimental protocol (complete experimental procedures are not required, but key experiments and/or indicators must be mentioned) to demonstrate that the bypass activation mediated by Protein X is distinguishable from the canonical pathway triggered by the binding of canonical EGFR ligands (such as EGF/TGF-α) to EGFR.", "session_data": {"scope_id": "6ae34df8fa9ee6736c938d963fc54899cb6c739a", "session_id": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "info": {"id": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "version": "local", "scopeID": "6ae34df8fa9ee6736c938d963fc54899cb6c739a", "directory": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8075__global/omb-batch", "title": "onemillion:natural_science/8075/global", "time": {"created": 1773731356331, "updated": 1773731460757}, "summary": {"additions": 0, "deletions": 0, "files": 0}}, "messages": [{"id": "msg_cfaa09ec0001RV3ZTNSkAQowS0", "info": {"id": "msg_cfaa09ec0001RV3ZTNSkAQowS0", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "role": "user", "time": {"created": 1773731356352}, "summary": {"title": "Demonstrating Bypass Activation of Protein X in Glioma", "diffs": []}, "agent": "synergy", "model": {"providerID": "sii-holos", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B"}}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfaa09ec1001Trd23YVXjYCDI5", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "messageID": "msg_cfaa09ec0001RV3ZTNSkAQowS0", "type": "text", "text": "\"In a C57BL/6 syngeneic (GL261 cells) orthotopic intracranial glioma model (30 days post-tumor establishment), a specific ligand-like molecule was significantly increased in the tumor group: the expression of gene α was upregulated, and its encoded product, Protein X, was also found at significantly elevated levels in the tumor tissue/tumor microenvironment. Preliminary results suggest that Protein X does not directly bind to EGFR but may activate the canonical downstream PI3K–AKT–mTOR pathway of EGFR via a bypass activation mechanism. Design a detailed experimental protocol (complete experimental procedures are not required, but key experiments and/or indicators must be mentioned) to demonstrate that the bypass activation mediated by Protein X is distinguishable from the canonical pathway triggered by the binding of canonical EGFR ligands (such as EGF/TGF-α) to EGFR.\"\n"}]}, {"id": "msg_cfaa09ef3001HPl9VrhCYhNC20", "info": {"id": "msg_cfaa09ef3001HPl9VrhCYhNC20", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "role": "assistant", "time": {"created": 1773731356403, "completed": 1773731460745}, "parentID": "msg_cfaa09ec0001RV3ZTNSkAQowS0", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B", "providerID": "sii-holos", "mode": "synergy", "agent": "synergy", "path": {"cwd": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8075__global/omb-batch", "root": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/natural_science__8075__global/omb-batch"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 25857, "output": 2717, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "finish": "stop"}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfaa0c3b6001VROBU0TAyWbadm", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "messageID": "msg_cfaa09ef3001HPl9VrhCYhNC20", "type": "step-start", "snapshot": "4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904"}, {"id": "prt_cfaa0c3b7001ONNnyOnu0AMQaG", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "messageID": "msg_cfaa09ef3001HPl9VrhCYhNC20", "type": "reasoning", "text": "This is a detailed scientific experimental design question about distinguishing bypass activation of EGFR downstream signaling from canonical ligand-mediated activation. Let me break down what's being asked:\n\n1. Context: C57BL/6 mouse glioma model (GL261 cells), orthotopic intracranial\n2. Observation: Gene α and Protein X are upregulated in tumor tissue\n3. Hypothesis: Protein X activates PI3K-AKT-mTOR pathway via bypass mechanism (not direct EGFR binding)\n4. Goal: Design experiments to distinguish this bypass from canonical EGF/TGF-α → EGFR → PI3K-AKT-mTOR activation\n\nKey experimental approaches to consider:\n\n1. **Binding studies** - Show Protein X doesn't bind EGFR directly (SPR, co-IP, pull-down)\n2. **Receptor activation status** - Compare EGFR phosphorylation patterns (canonical ligands cause specific tyrosine phosphorylation; bypass may not)\n3. **Downstream signaling kinetics** - Different temporal patterns of AKT/mTOR activation\n4. **Inhibitor sensitivity** - Different sensitivity to EGFR kinase inhibitors vs downstream inhibitors\n5. **Genetic manipulation** - EGFR knockout/knockdown should block canonical but not bypass\n6. **Intermediate receptor identification** - What receptor does Protein X actually bind?\n7. **Spatial signaling** - Different subcellular localization of signaling complexes\n8. **Transcriptomic signatures** - Different gene expression profiles from canonical vs bypass\n\nLet me design a comprehensive experimental protocol with these key components.", "time": {"start": 1773731365815, "end": 1773731460730}}, {"id": "prt_cfaa108e7001WDpR2XEsgY1O20", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "messageID": "msg_cfaa09ef3001HPl9VrhCYhNC20", "type": "text", "text": "\n\n# Experimental Protocol: Distinguishing Protein X-Mediated Bypass Activation from Canonical EGFR Ligand Signaling\n\n## Overview\n\nThis protocol is designed to demonstrate that Protein X activates the PI3K–AKT–mTOR pathway through a **bypass mechanism** that is mechanistically distinguishable from canonical EGFR ligand (EGF/TGF-α) signaling. The experimental strategy focuses on four key discriminators:\n\n| Discriminator | Canonical (EGF/TGF-α) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| EGFR binding | Direct | None |\n| EGFR phosphorylation | Tyr1068/1173 ↑ | Minimal/absent |\n| EGFR kinase inhibitor sensitivity | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| EGFR dependency | Required | Dispensable |\n\n---\n\n## Experimental Design\n\n### **Aim 1: Demonstrate Protein X Does Not Directly Bind EGFR**\n\n| Experiment | Key Readout | Expected Outcome (Bypass) |\n|-----------|-------------|--------------------------|\n| **Surface Plasmon Resonance (SPR)** | Binding affinity (KD) | No detectable binding between recombinant Protein X and EGFR extracellular domain |\n| **Co-immunoprecipitation** | EGFR–Protein X complex | No co-IP in GL261 cells or tumor lysates |\n| **Ligand-binding competition assay** | Displacement of ¹²⁵I-EGF | Protein X fails to compete with EGF for EGFR binding |\n| **Cellular thermal shift assay (CETSA)** | EGFR thermal stabilization | Protein X does not stabilize EGFR (unlike EGF) |\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 2: Compare EGFR Activation Status**\n\nCanonical EGFR ligands induce **specific tyrosine autophosphorylation patterns**. Bypass activation should show a distinct signature.\n\n| Experiment | Key Readout | Distinguishing Feature |\n|-----------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **Phospho-EGFR Western blot** | pY1068, pY1173, pY992, pY1045 | EGF: strong phosphorylation; Protein X: minimal/no phosphorylation |\n| **EGFR phospho-tyrosine mass spectrometry** | Comprehensive pY profiling | Different phosphorylation site repertoire |\n| **EGFR dimerization assay (BSFRET/crosslinking)** | Receptor oligomerization | EGF induces dimerization; Protein X may not |\n| **EGFR internalization assay** | Surface EGFR downregulation | EGF causes rapid internalization; Protein X may not |\n\n**Key antibodies to use:**\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y1068) – Grb2 binding site\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y1173) – Shc binding site\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y992) – PLCγ binding site\n- Anti-total EGFR\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 3: Differential Sensitivity to EGFR Pathway Inhibitors**\n\nThis is a **critical discriminator** – bypass activation should be resistant to upstream inhibition.\n\n| Inhibitor Class | Specific Agent | Target | Canonical (EGF) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|----------------|----------------|--------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| **EGFR kinase inhibitor** | Erlotinib/Gefitinib | EGFR kinase domain | **Blocks** pAKT | **No effect** on pAKT |\n| **EGFR neutralizing antibody** | Cetuximab/Panitumumab | EGFR extracellular domain | **Blocks** pAKT | **No effect** on pAKT |\n| **PI3K inhibitor** | LY294002/BKM120 | PI3K catalytic subunit | Blocks pAKT | Blocks pAKT |\n| **AKT inhibitor** | MK-2206 | AKT kinase domain | Blocks pS6 | Blocks pS6 |\n| **mTOR inhibitor** | Rapamycin/Everolimus | mTORC1 | Blocks pS6 | Blocks pS6 |\n\n**Experimental setup:**\n- Treat GL261 cells (± Protein X stimulation or EGF stimulation) with inhibitors\n- Measure: pAKT (S473), pS6 (S235/236), p4EBP1 by Western blot\n- **Key criterion:** Protein X-induced pAKT persists despite EGFR inhibition\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 4: Genetic Dissection of EGFR Dependency**\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Expected Outcome (Bypass) |\n|-----------|----------|--------------------------|\n| **EGFR knockout** | CRISPR/Cas9 in GL261 cells | EGF signaling abolished; Protein X signaling **preserved** |\n| **EGFR knockdown** | shRNA/siRNA | EGF signaling reduced; Protein X signaling **unaffected** |\n| **EGFR rescue** | Re-express wild-type vs kinase-dead EGFR | Protein X signaling independent of EGFR status |\n| **Dominant-negative EGFR** | Express EGFR-CD533 (truncated) | Blocks EGF signaling; **no effect** on Protein X |\n\n**Readouts:** pAKT, pS6, cell proliferation, survival assays\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 5: Identify the True Receptor for Protein X**\n\nSince Protein X activates PI3K–AKT–mTOR without EGFR, it must signal through an **alternative receptor**.\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Purpose |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **Protein X pull-down + MS** | Biotinylated Protein X → streptavidin pulldown → LC-MS/MS | Identify binding partners |\n| **Expression screen** | siRNA library against RTKs/GPCRs | Identify receptor required for Protein X signaling |\n| **Phospho-RTK array** | Compare EGF vs Protein X stimulation | Identify which RTKs are activated by Protein X |\n| **Candidate validation** | Knockout/knockdown of candidate receptors | Confirm requirement for Protein X signaling |\n\n**Candidate receptors to prioritize:**\n- Other ErbB family members (HER2/HER3)\n- MET, AXL, PDGFR (known to activate PI3K–AKT)\n- GPCRs that transactivate PI3K (Gβγ-mediated)\n- Integrins (FAK/Src-mediated PI3K activation)\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 6: Signaling Kinetics and Amplitude Comparison**\n\nCanonical and bypass pathways often show **distinct temporal dynamics**.\n\n| Parameter | Measurement | Distinguishing Value |\n|-----------|-------------|---------------------|\n| **Activation kinetics** | pAKT time course (0, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120 min) | EGF: rapid peak (5–15 min); Protein X: may be slower/sustained |\n| **Signal amplitude** | pAKT dose-response | Different EC50 and Emax |\n| **Signal duration** | pAKT after washout | EGF: rapid decay; Protein X: may persist |\n| **Feedback activation** | pERK, pS6K over time | Different feedback loop engagement |\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 7: Transcriptomic Signature Comparison**\n\nCanonical EGFR signaling and bypass activation may drive **distinct gene expression programs**.\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Readout |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **RNA-seq** | GL261 ± EGF ± Protein X (4–8 hr) | Differentially expressed genes |\n| **GSEA** | Compare pathway enrichment | EGFR signature vs alternative RTK signature |\n| **Immediate early genes** | qPCR for FOS, JUN, EGR1 | Different induction patterns |\n\n**Expected:** Protein X induces a transcriptional program distinct from EGF, reflecting different upstream activators.\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 8: In Vivo Validation in GL261 Orthotopic Model**\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Key Readout |\n|-----------|----------|-------------|\n| **EGFR inhibitor treatment** | Erlotinib in tumor-bearing mice | Tumor growth, survival, pAKT in tumor tissue |\n| **PI3K inhibitor treatment** | BKM120 in tumor-bearing mice | Tumor growth, survival, pAKT in tumor tissue |\n| **Protein X neutralization** | Anti-Protein X antibody | Tumor growth, pAKT reduction |\n| **Combined targeting** | EGFRi + anti-Protein X | Additive/synergistic effect suggests independent pathways |\n| **IHC analysis** | pEGFR, pAKT, pS6 in tumor sections | Spatial correlation of Protein X with pAKT but not pEGFR |\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Discriminators\n\n| Criterion | Canonical (EGF/TGF-α) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|-----------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| **Direct EGFR binding** | ✓ | ✗ |\n| **EGFR phosphorylation** | Strong (Y1068, Y1173) | Minimal/absent |\n| **EGFR kinase inhibitor** | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| **EGFR neutralizing antibody** | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| **PI3K/AKT/mTOR inhibitors** | Sensitive | Sensitive |\n| **EGFR knockout** | Abolishes signaling | Signaling preserved |\n| **Alternative receptor** | Not required | Required (to be identified) |\n| **Signaling kinetics** | Rapid, transient | May differ |\n| **Transcriptional signature** | EGFR-dependent | Distinct |\n\n---\n\n## Critical Controls\n\n1. **Positive control:** EGF stimulation (canonical pathway)\n2. **Negative control:** Vehicle treatment\n3. **Specificity control:** Protein X from α-knockout cells/tissue\n4. **Off-target control:** Use ≥2 inhibitors per target class\n5. **Genetic control:** ≥2 independent sgRNAs/shRNAs per target\n\n---\n\n## Expected Conclusions\n\nIf Protein X mediates bypass activation, the data should show:\n\n1. **No direct EGFR binding** (Aim 1)\n2. **No EGFR phosphorylation** despite strong pAKT (Aim 2)\n3. **Resistance to EGFR inhibitors** but sensitivity to PI3K/AKT/mTOR inhibitors (Aim 3)\n4. **Preserved signaling in EGFR-KO cells** (Aim 4)\n5. **Identification of an alternative receptor** (Aim 5)\n\nThis would establish Protein X as activating PI3K–AKT–mTOR through a **mechanistically distinct bypass pathway**, with implications for therapeutic targeting in glioma.", "time": {"start": 1773731460731, "end": 1773731460731}}, {"id": "prt_cfaa2367e001aMDuyqo6940q3X", "sessionID": "ses_3055f6154ffetUe5ghHDFd2BkO", "messageID": "msg_cfaa09ef3001HPl9VrhCYhNC20", "type": "step-finish", "reason": "stop", "snapshot": "4b825dc642cb6eb9a060e54bf8d69288fbee4904", "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 25857, "output": 2717, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}}]}]}, "result": {"answer": "# Experimental Protocol: Distinguishing Protein X-Mediated Bypass Activation from Canonical EGFR Ligand Signaling\n\n## Overview\n\nThis protocol is designed to demonstrate that Protein X activates the PI3K–AKT–mTOR pathway through a **bypass mechanism** that is mechanistically distinguishable from canonical EGFR ligand (EGF/TGF-α) signaling. The experimental strategy focuses on four key discriminators:\n\n| Discriminator | Canonical (EGF/TGF-α) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| EGFR binding | Direct | None |\n| EGFR phosphorylation | Tyr1068/1173 ↑ | Minimal/absent |\n| EGFR kinase inhibitor sensitivity | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| EGFR dependency | Required | Dispensable |\n\n---\n\n## Experimental Design\n\n### **Aim 1: Demonstrate Protein X Does Not Directly Bind EGFR**\n\n| Experiment | Key Readout | Expected Outcome (Bypass) |\n|-----------|-------------|--------------------------|\n| **Surface Plasmon Resonance (SPR)** | Binding affinity (KD) | No detectable binding between recombinant Protein X and EGFR extracellular domain |\n| **Co-immunoprecipitation** | EGFR–Protein X complex | No co-IP in GL261 cells or tumor lysates |\n| **Ligand-binding competition assay** | Displacement of ¹²⁵I-EGF | Protein X fails to compete with EGF for EGFR binding |\n| **Cellular thermal shift assay (CETSA)** | EGFR thermal stabilization | Protein X does not stabilize EGFR (unlike EGF) |\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 2: Compare EGFR Activation Status**\n\nCanonical EGFR ligands induce **specific tyrosine autophosphorylation patterns**. Bypass activation should show a distinct signature.\n\n| Experiment | Key Readout | Distinguishing Feature |\n|-----------|-------------|----------------------|\n| **Phospho-EGFR Western blot** | pY1068, pY1173, pY992, pY1045 | EGF: strong phosphorylation; Protein X: minimal/no phosphorylation |\n| **EGFR phospho-tyrosine mass spectrometry** | Comprehensive pY profiling | Different phosphorylation site repertoire |\n| **EGFR dimerization assay (BSFRET/crosslinking)** | Receptor oligomerization | EGF induces dimerization; Protein X may not |\n| **EGFR internalization assay** | Surface EGFR downregulation | EGF causes rapid internalization; Protein X may not |\n\n**Key antibodies to use:**\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y1068) – Grb2 binding site\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y1173) – Shc binding site\n- Anti-pEGFR (Y992) – PLCγ binding site\n- Anti-total EGFR\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 3: Differential Sensitivity to EGFR Pathway Inhibitors**\n\nThis is a **critical discriminator** – bypass activation should be resistant to upstream inhibition.\n\n| Inhibitor Class | Specific Agent | Target | Canonical (EGF) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|----------------|----------------|--------|-----------------|-------------------|\n| **EGFR kinase inhibitor** | Erlotinib/Gefitinib | EGFR kinase domain | **Blocks** pAKT | **No effect** on pAKT |\n| **EGFR neutralizing antibody** | Cetuximab/Panitumumab | EGFR extracellular domain | **Blocks** pAKT | **No effect** on pAKT |\n| **PI3K inhibitor** | LY294002/BKM120 | PI3K catalytic subunit | Blocks pAKT | Blocks pAKT |\n| **AKT inhibitor** | MK-2206 | AKT kinase domain | Blocks pS6 | Blocks pS6 |\n| **mTOR inhibitor** | Rapamycin/Everolimus | mTORC1 | Blocks pS6 | Blocks pS6 |\n\n**Experimental setup:**\n- Treat GL261 cells (± Protein X stimulation or EGF stimulation) with inhibitors\n- Measure: pAKT (S473), pS6 (S235/236), p4EBP1 by Western blot\n- **Key criterion:** Protein X-induced pAKT persists despite EGFR inhibition\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 4: Genetic Dissection of EGFR Dependency**\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Expected Outcome (Bypass) |\n|-----------|----------|--------------------------|\n| **EGFR knockout** | CRISPR/Cas9 in GL261 cells | EGF signaling abolished; Protein X signaling **preserved** |\n| **EGFR knockdown** | shRNA/siRNA | EGF signaling reduced; Protein X signaling **unaffected** |\n| **EGFR rescue** | Re-express wild-type vs kinase-dead EGFR | Protein X signaling independent of EGFR status |\n| **Dominant-negative EGFR** | Express EGFR-CD533 (truncated) | Blocks EGF signaling; **no effect** on Protein X |\n\n**Readouts:** pAKT, pS6, cell proliferation, survival assays\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 5: Identify the True Receptor for Protein X**\n\nSince Protein X activates PI3K–AKT–mTOR without EGFR, it must signal through an **alternative receptor**.\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Purpose |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **Protein X pull-down + MS** | Biotinylated Protein X → streptavidin pulldown → LC-MS/MS | Identify binding partners |\n| **Expression screen** | siRNA library against RTKs/GPCRs | Identify receptor required for Protein X signaling |\n| **Phospho-RTK array** | Compare EGF vs Protein X stimulation | Identify which RTKs are activated by Protein X |\n| **Candidate validation** | Knockout/knockdown of candidate receptors | Confirm requirement for Protein X signaling |\n\n**Candidate receptors to prioritize:**\n- Other ErbB family members (HER2/HER3)\n- MET, AXL, PDGFR (known to activate PI3K–AKT)\n- GPCRs that transactivate PI3K (Gβγ-mediated)\n- Integrins (FAK/Src-mediated PI3K activation)\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 6: Signaling Kinetics and Amplitude Comparison**\n\nCanonical and bypass pathways often show **distinct temporal dynamics**.\n\n| Parameter | Measurement | Distinguishing Value |\n|-----------|-------------|---------------------|\n| **Activation kinetics** | pAKT time course (0, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120 min) | EGF: rapid peak (5–15 min); Protein X: may be slower/sustained |\n| **Signal amplitude** | pAKT dose-response | Different EC50 and Emax |\n| **Signal duration** | pAKT after washout | EGF: rapid decay; Protein X: may persist |\n| **Feedback activation** | pERK, pS6K over time | Different feedback loop engagement |\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 7: Transcriptomic Signature Comparison**\n\nCanonical EGFR signaling and bypass activation may drive **distinct gene expression programs**.\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Readout |\n|-----------|----------|---------|\n| **RNA-seq** | GL261 ± EGF ± Protein X (4–8 hr) | Differentially expressed genes |\n| **GSEA** | Compare pathway enrichment | EGFR signature vs alternative RTK signature |\n| **Immediate early genes** | qPCR for FOS, JUN, EGR1 | Different induction patterns |\n\n**Expected:** Protein X induces a transcriptional program distinct from EGF, reflecting different upstream activators.\n\n---\n\n### **Aim 8: In Vivo Validation in GL261 Orthotopic Model**\n\n| Experiment | Approach | Key Readout |\n|-----------|----------|-------------|\n| **EGFR inhibitor treatment** | Erlotinib in tumor-bearing mice | Tumor growth, survival, pAKT in tumor tissue |\n| **PI3K inhibitor treatment** | BKM120 in tumor-bearing mice | Tumor growth, survival, pAKT in tumor tissue |\n| **Protein X neutralization** | Anti-Protein X antibody | Tumor growth, pAKT reduction |\n| **Combined targeting** | EGFRi + anti-Protein X | Additive/synergistic effect suggests independent pathways |\n| **IHC analysis** | pEGFR, pAKT, pS6 in tumor sections | Spatial correlation of Protein X with pAKT but not pEGFR |\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Discriminators\n\n| Criterion | Canonical (EGF/TGF-α) | Bypass (Protein X) |\n|-----------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| **Direct EGFR binding** | ✓ | ✗ |\n| **EGFR phosphorylation** | Strong (Y1068, Y1173) | Minimal/absent |\n| **EGFR kinase inhibitor** | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| **EGFR neutralizing antibody** | Sensitive | Resistant |\n| **PI3K/AKT/mTOR inhibitors** | Sensitive | Sensitive |\n| **EGFR knockout** | Abolishes signaling | Signaling preserved |\n| **Alternative receptor** | Not required | Required (to be identified) |\n| **Signaling kinetics** | Rapid, transient | May differ |\n| **Transcriptional signature** | EGFR-dependent | Distinct |\n\n---\n\n## Critical Controls\n\n1. **Positive control:** EGF stimulation (canonical pathway)\n2. **Negative control:** Vehicle treatment\n3. **Specificity control:** Protein X from α-knockout cells/tissue\n4. **Off-target control:** Use ≥2 inhibitors per target class\n5. **Genetic control:** ≥2 independent sgRNAs/shRNAs per target\n\n---\n\n## Expected Conclusions\n\nIf Protein X mediates bypass activation, the data should show:\n\n1. **No direct EGFR binding** (Aim 1)\n2. **No EGFR phosphorylation** despite strong pAKT (Aim 2)\n3. **Resistance to EGFR inhibitors** but sensitivity to PI3K/AKT/mTOR inhibitors (Aim 3)\n4. **Preserved signaling in EGFR-KO cells** (Aim 4)\n5. **Identification of an alternative receptor** (Aim 5)\n\nThis would establish Protein X as activating PI3K–AKT–mTOR through a **mechanistically distinct bypass pathway**, with implications for therapeutic targeting in glioma.", "case_id": 8075, "language": "global", "tags": {"topics": ["Natural Sciences", "Biology", "Molecular Biology"], "time_sensitivity": {"time_sensitivity": "Time-agnostic", "year_month": "NA", "day": "NA"}}, "rubric_count": 17}, "metrics": {"solve_time_seconds": 107.0, "tokens": {"input": 25857, "output": 2717, "total": 28574}, "cost": 0.0, "step_count": 1}, "error": ""}}
{"task_id": "healthcare_and_medicine/9890/cn", "answer": "我无法访问外部网络资源来获取《重症肺结核诊断和治疗专家共识》（2025版）的具体内容。但我可以基于现有的重症肺结核、ARDS合并药物性肝损伤的临床治疗原则，为您提供一个综合诊疗方案。\n\n**重要说明**：由于无法获取2025版专家共识的具体内容，以下方案基于重症肺结核、ARDS及药物性肝损伤的通用临床治疗原则制定。**强烈建议您在实施前对照2025版专家共识原文进行核实和调整**。\n\n---\n\n## 综合诊疗方案\n\n### 一、病情评估与优先级\n\n该患者属于**危重症肺结核合并多器官功能障碍**：\n- **呼吸衰竭**：重度ARDS（P/F=95），机械通气中\n- **循环衰竭**：脓毒性休克，需血管活性药物维持\n- **代谢衰竭**：重度营养不良（BMI 16.5）\n- **肝功能受损**：ALT 3×ULN，有长期饮酒史\n- **合并真菌感染**：疑似侵袭性肺曲霉病（IPA）\n\n**治疗优先级**：\n1. 生命支持（呼吸、循环）\n2. 抗感染治疗（抗结核+抗真菌）\n3. 肝功能保护与药物调整\n4. 营养支持\n\n---\n\n### 二、药物治疗方案\n\n#### （一）抗结核治疗方案调整\n\n**当前问题分析**：\n- 患者ALT 125 U/L（3×ULN），总胆红素升高，存在药物性肝损伤（DILI）\n- 标准四联方案（HRZE）中，**异烟肼(H)、利福平(R)、吡嗪酰胺(Z)** 均为肝毒性药物\n- 根据DILI处理原则，ALT>3×ULN伴症状或ALT>5×ULN时应停用肝毒性药物\n\n**建议调整方案**：\n\n| 阶段 | 方案组成 | 剂量与用法 | 疗程 |\n|------|----------|------------|------|\n| **强化期**（肝功能恢复前） | **左氧氟沙星 + 乙胺丁醇 + 利奈唑胺 + 阿米卡星** | 左氧氟沙星 750mg QD（静脉）<br>乙胺丁醇 0.75g QD（鼻饲）<br>利奈唑胺 600mg BID（静脉/鼻饲）<br>阿米卡星 0.4g QD（静脉，根据肾功能调整） | 2-4周，直至肝功能恢复 |\n| **强化期**（肝功能恢复后） | **利福平 + 异烟肼 + 乙胺丁醇 + 吡嗪酰胺** | 利福平 0.45g QD<br>异烟肼 0.3g QD + 维生素B6 30mg QD<br>乙胺丁醇 0.75g QD<br>吡嗪酰胺 1.0g QD（减量） | 至少2个月 |\n| **继续期** | **利福平 + 异烟肼 + 乙胺丁醇** | 利福平 0.45g QD<br>异烟肼 0.3g QD<br>乙胺丁醇 0.75g QD | 总疗程≥12个月 |\n\n**关键调整说明**：\n1. **立即停用**：吡嗪酰胺（肝毒性最强）、异烟肼、利福平\n2. **保留**：乙胺丁醇（肝毒性最小）\n3. **添加**：\n   - 左氧氟沙星（氟喹诺酮类，二线抗结核主力）\n   - 利奈唑胺（对重症/耐药结核有效，但需监测骨髓抑制）\n   - 阿米卡星（注射用氨基糖苷类，强化杀菌）\n4. **保肝治疗**：\n   - 谷胱甘肽 1.2g QD 静脉滴注\n   - 多烯磷脂酰胆碱 465mg TID 鼻饲\n   - 必要时加用异甘草酸镁\n\n**肝功能恢复标准**：ALT<2×ULN，总胆红素正常，无症状\n\n#### （二）抗真菌治疗方案\n\n**当前问题**：\n- 伏立康唑经肝脏代谢，肝功能受损时需调整剂量\n- 重症患者伏立康唑血药浓度波动大，需治疗药物监测（TDM）\n\n**建议方案**：\n\n| 药物 | 剂量调整 | 监测要求 |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| **伏立康唑** | 负荷剂量：6mg/kg Q12h × 2次<br>维持剂量：100mg BID（肝功能受损减量） | **必须行TDM监测**<br>目标谷浓度：1-5.5 μg/mL<br>给药后第5天达稳态时首次检测 |\n\n**替代方案**（如伏立康唑不耐受或TDM不达标）：\n- **艾沙康唑**：200mg TID × 6次后，200mg QD（肝毒性较小，无需常规TDM）\n- **两性霉素B脂质体**：3-5mg/kg QD（肾功能允许时）\n\n#### （三）ARDS与脓毒性休克支持治疗\n\n| 治疗类别 | 具体措施 |\n|----------|----------|\n| **肺保护性通气** | 潮气量 6-8 mL/kg（理想体重）<br>平台压<30 cmH₂O<br>PEEP 根据PEEP-FiO₂表设置<br>允许性高碳酸血症（pH>7.20） |\n| **俯卧位通气** | 每日≥12小时（P/F<150时强烈推荐） |\n| **液体管理** | 限制性液体策略<br>目标：CVP 8-12 mmHg，尿量>0.5 mL/kg/h |\n| **血管活性药物** | 去甲肾上腺素为一线（优于多巴胺）<br>目标MAP≥65 mmHg |\n| **糖皮质激素** | 氢化可的松 200mg/日 持续静脉泵入（脓毒性休克）<br>或甲泼尼龙 1-2mg/kg/日（ARDS，争议中） |\n\n#### （四）营养支持治疗\n\n**患者BMI 16.5，属重度营养不良，需积极营养支持**：\n\n| 阶段 | 目标 | 方案 |\n|------|------|------|\n| **起始期**（1-3天） | 20-25 kcal/kg/日<br>蛋白 1.2-1.5 g/kg/日 | 肠内营养优先（鼻饲）<br>起始速率 20-30 mL/h<br>逐步递增 |\n| **目标期**（4-7天） | 30-35 kcal/kg/日<br>蛋白 1.5-2.0 g/kg/日 | 整蛋白配方 + 免疫营养素（ω-3脂肪酸、精氨酸）<br>必要时补充肠外营养 |\n| **监测** | 每日评估耐受性 | 胃残余量<250mL<br>监测电解质（警惕再喂养综合征） |\n\n**补充**：\n- 维生素B6 30mg QD（预防异烟肼周围神经炎）\n- 维生素K1 10mg QD（肝功能受损时）\n- 微量元素补充（锌、硒）\n\n---\n\n### 三、风险管理与监测计划\n\n#### （一）药物性肝损伤（DILI）监测\n\n| 监测项目 | 频率 | 警戒值 | 处理措施 |\n|----------|------|--------|----------|\n| ALT/AST | Q1-2日 | >5×ULN 或 >3×ULN伴症状 | 停所有肝毒性药物 |\n| 总胆红素 | Q1-2日 | >2×ULN | 评估是否需要人工肝支持 |\n| 凝血功能(PT/INR) | Q2-3日 | INR>1.5 | 维生素K1，必要时血浆 |\n| 血氨 | 每周 | 升高 | 警惕肝性脑病 |\n\n**DILI再挑战原则**：\n- 肝功能恢复正常后，逐个 reintroduce 抗结核药\n- 顺序：乙胺丁醇 → 利福平 → 异烟肼 → 吡嗪酰胺（最后考虑，可永久停用）\n- 每加一种药后监测肝功能3-5天\n\n#### （二）抗结核药物不良反应监测\n\n| 药物 | 主要毒性 | 监测项目 | 频率 |\n|------|----------|----------|------|\n| 左氧氟沙星 | QT延长、肌腱炎 | 心电图、跟腱症状 | 基线+每周 |\n| 利奈唑胺 | 骨髓抑制、周围神经炎 | 血常规、神经系统评估 | Q3-5日 |\n| 阿米卡星 | 耳毒性、肾毒性 | 听力、肾功能、尿常规 | Q2-3日 |\n| 乙胺丁醇 | 视神经炎 | 视力、色觉 | 基线+每月 |\n\n#### （三）伏立康唑治疗药物监测（TDM）\n\n| 时间点 | 目标 | 处理 |\n|--------|------|------|\n| 首次检测 | 给药后第5天（达稳态） | 谷浓度（下次给药前） |\n| 目标范围 | 1-5.5 μg/mL | <1：增加剂量<br>>5.5：减量或停药 |\n| 复查频率 | 剂量调整后1周；稳定后每月 | 肝功能变化时随时复查 |\n\n#### （四）感染与疗效监测\n\n| 监测项目 | 频率 | 目标/评估 |\n|----------|------|-----------|\n| 痰涂片抗酸染色 | 每周 | 转阴趋势 |\n| 痰培养+药敏 | 每2-4周 | 菌量减少、药敏指导 |\n| 痰真菌培养/G试验 | 每2周 | 曲霉菌清除 |\n| 胸部CT | 每2-4周 | 空洞吸收、渗出减少 |\n| 炎症指标(CRP/PCT) | Q2-3日 | 下降趋势 |\n| 血气分析 | QD-BID | P/F比值改善 |\n\n#### （五）营养与代谢监测\n\n| 监测项目 | 频率 | 目标 |\n|----------|------|------|\n| 体重/BMI | 每周 | 逐步增加 |\n| 前白蛋白 | 每周 | 上升趋势 |\n| 电解质(K/Mg/P) | Q1-2日（起始期） | 正常范围 |\n| 血糖 | Q4-6h | 7.8-10 mmol/L |\n\n---\n\n### 四、预警与升级处理\n\n| 情况 | 预警信号 | 升级处理 |\n|------|----------|----------|\n| **肝功能恶化** | ALT>10×ULN 或 胆红素>5×ULN | 停用所有可疑药物，考虑人工肝支持 |\n| **呼吸衰竭加重** | P/F<80 或 平台压>35 cmH₂O | 评估ECMO指征 |\n| **休克难纠正** | 去甲肾上腺素>0.5 μg/kg/min | 加用血管加压素，评估肾上腺功能 |\n| **大咯血** | 一次>100mL 或 24h>500mL | 支气管动脉栓塞术(BAE) |\n| **真菌感染进展** | G试验持续升高或新发病灶 | 升级抗真菌方案（两性霉素B脂质体） |\n\n---\n\n### 五、患者及家属沟通要点\n\n1. **病情危重性**：重症肺结核合并ARDS、脓毒性休克，死亡率高\n2. **治疗长期性**：抗结核疗程≥12个月，需长期住院或转专科\n3. **药物调整必要性**：肝功能受损需频繁调整方案，可能影响疗效\n4. **经济负担**：伏立康唑TDM、利奈唑胺等费用较高\n5. **预后评估**：即使存活，可能遗留肺功能损害\n\n---\n\n**重要提醒**：本方案基于通用临床原则制定，**必须对照《重症肺结核诊断和治疗专家共识》（2025版）原文进行核实**。建议您：\n1. 获取2025版专家共识全文\n2. 邀请呼吸与危重症医学科、感染科、临床药学多学科会诊\n3. 根据患者具体病情变化动态调整方案", "score": {"rubric_results": [{"rubric_number": 1, "weight": -8, "met": false, "reason": "模型明确建议立即停用异烟肼、利福平和吡嗪酰胺，未出现 rubric 描述的未建议停药情况。"}, {"rubric_number": 2, "weight": 7, "met": true, "reason": "模型明确指出因患者 ALT 达 3 倍正常值上限，符合肝损伤停药标准，建议停用相关药物。"}, {"rubric_number": 3, "weight": 6, "met": false, "reason": "模型未提及利福平与伏立康唑之间的药物相互作用及禁止联用，仅因肝毒性建议停用利福平。"}, {"rubric_number": 4, "weight": 7, "met": false, "reason": "模型虽建议部分药物改为静脉给药，但未明确分析胃肠功能障碍及鼻饲吸收不可靠的原因。"}, {"rubric_number": 5, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型方案中明确包含利奈唑胺 600mg BID（静脉/鼻饲），符合剂量和频次要求。"}, {"rubric_number": 6, "weight": 5, "met": true, "reason": "模型建议使用左氧氟沙星 750mg QD 静脉滴注，符合要求。"}, {"rubric_number": 7, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型明确保留乙胺丁醇，并说明其肝毒性最小。"}, {"rubric_number": 8, "weight": 3, "met": false, "reason": "模型建议添加阿米卡星，未出现 rubric 描述的暂不添加情况。"}, {"rubric_number": 9, "weight": -4, "met": false, "reason": "模型将药物治疗方案与风险管理计划分章节清晰列出，逻辑结构清晰。"}, {"rubric_number": 10, "weight": 5, "met": false, "reason": "模型回复中未提及密闭式吸痰装置或呼吸机回路过滤器等防气溶胶传播措施。"}, {"rubric_number": 11, "weight": 3, "met": true, "reason": "模型在保肝治疗中明确列举了异甘草酸镁。"}, {"rubric_number": 12, "weight": -5, "met": false, "reason": "模型明确建议去甲肾上腺素为一线，优于多巴胺，未出现 rubric 描述的未建议更换情况。"}, {"rubric_number": 13, "weight": 3, "met": false, "reason": "模型设定的停药指征为 ALT>5×ULN 或 ALT>3×ULN 伴症状，未提及总胆红素大于 3 倍正常值上限这一指征。"}, {"rubric_number": 14, "weight": 4, "met": false, "reason": "模型虽建议起始低热量营养，但未明确使用“允许性低热量”术语或明确关联休克状态。"}, {"rubric_number": 15, "weight": -3, "met": false, "reason": "模型回复针对患者具体病情制定方案，未包含大量通用病理生理学科普内容。"}], "score": 23, "max_score": 51, "raw_response": "[\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 1,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确建议立即停用异烟肼、利福平和吡嗪酰胺，未出现 rubric 描述的未建议停药情况。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 2,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确指出因患者 ALT 达 3 倍正常值上限，符合肝损伤停药标准，建议停用相关药物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 3,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型未提及利福平与伏立康唑之间的药物相互作用及禁止联用，仅因肝毒性建议停用利福平。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 4,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型虽建议部分药物改为静脉给药，但未明确分析胃肠功能障碍及鼻饲吸收不可靠的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 5,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型方案中明确包含利奈唑胺 600mg BID（静脉/鼻饲），符合剂量和频次要求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 6,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型建议使用左氧氟沙星 750mg QD 静脉滴注，符合要求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 7,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确保留乙胺丁醇，并说明其肝毒性最小。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 8,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型建议添加阿米卡星，未出现 rubric 描述的暂不添加情况。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 9,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型将药物治疗方案与风险管理计划分章节清晰列出，逻辑结构清晰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 10,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型回复中未提及密闭式吸痰装置或呼吸机回路过滤器等防气溶胶传播措施。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 11,\n    \"status\": \"是\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型在保肝治疗中明确列举了异甘草酸镁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 12,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型明确建议去甲肾上腺素为一线，优于多巴胺，未出现 rubric 描述的未建议更换情况。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 13,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型设定的停药指征为 ALT>5×ULN 或 ALT>3×ULN 伴症状，未提及总胆红素大于 3 倍正常值上限这一指征。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 14,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型虽建议起始低热量营养，但未明确使用“允许性低热量”术语或明确关联休克状态。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"rubric_id\": 15,\n    \"status\": \"否\",\n    \"justification\": \"模型回复针对患者具体病情制定方案，未包含大量通用病理生理学科普内容。\"\n  }\n]"}, "error": null, "stage": null, "system_prompt": "You are a domain expert capable of delivering professional-grade responses in both English and 中文.\n\n## Core Rules\n\n1. **Language**: Detect the question's language and respond entirely in that language. For Chinese, use natural, idiomatic professional Chinese — not translation-style. Never mix languages unless a term has no established translation.\n\n2. **Role**: If the question assigns a role, adopt it fully. If not, infer the appropriate expert identity from the scenario.\n\n3. **Scenario Focus**: Address the specific scenario directly. Do not provide generic domain overviews.\n\n4. **Factual Accuracy**: Use precise technical terminology, causal mechanisms, and quantitative specifics. Distinguish consensus from speculation.\n\n5. **Analytical Depth**: Decompose problems logically. Compare options with explicit dimensions and trade-offs. Explain \"why\" and \"how,\" not just \"what.\" Consider edge cases and real-world constraints.\n\n6. **Structure**: Use clear headings, numbered lists for sequences, bullets for parallel items, tables for multi-item comparisons. Lead with the key answer, then elaborate. End longer responses with a summary.\n\n7. **Instruction Following**: Address ALL sub-questions explicitly. Honor any specified constraints exactly.\n\n8. **Prohibitions**: Never fabricate data or citations. Never ignore parts of the question. Never be unnecessarily verbose. Never respond in the wrong language.", "user_prompt": "患者基本情况\n患者：45岁，男性。BMI 16.5 kg/m²（重度营养不良），神志模糊（GCS 13分），血压 85/50 mmHg（多巴胺维持中）。\n \n核心诊断：\n重症肺结核（III型 危重症型）：双肺广泛空洞破坏，合并脓毒性休克。\n重度急性呼吸窘迫综合征（ARDS）：PaO₂/FiO₂ = 95 mmHg，目前气管插管机械通气中。\n药物性肝损伤（DILI）高风险：既往有长期饮酒史，入院查 ALT 125 U/L（3倍正常值上限），总胆红素 38 μmol/L。\n疑似侵袭性肺曲霉病：痰培养提示曲霉菌属阳性，G试验阳性。\n \n当前用药（外院带入）：利福平 0.45g QD（鼻饲）、异烟肼 0.3g QD（鼻饲）、