/monthly inspection items, dimensions for data review, and fault contingency plans).", "session_data": {"scope_id": "39b0127db496df170bab2473d2ee4511f024894f", "session_id": "ses_30561d25bffemch6DJHdq1yXPx", "info": {"id": "ses_30561d25bffemch6DJHdq1yXPx", "version": "local", "scopeID": "39b0127db496df170bab2473d2ee4511f024894f", "directory": "/inspire/hdd/project/multi-agent/niexiaohang-25130061/holos-synergy/benchmark/workspaces/onemillion/industry__9705__global/omb-batch", "title": "onemillion:industry/9705/global", "time": {"created": 1773731196324, "updated": 1773731389916}, "summary": {"additions": 0, "deletions": 0, "files": 0}}, "messages": [{"id": "msg_cfa9e2dba001u083KfeG6aUreJ", "info": {"id": "msg_cfa9e2dba001u083KfeG6aUreJ", "sessionID": "ses_30561d25bffemch6DJHdq1yXPx", "role": "user", "time": {"created": 1773731196346}, "summary": {"title": "Automotive line connectivity issue troubleshooting", "diffs": []}, "agent": "synergy", "model": {"providerID": "sii-holos", "modelID": "Qwen 3.5 397B A17B"}}, "parts": [{"id": "prt_cfa9e2dbb001ZWxyovFtTEq8xG", "sessionID": "ses_30561d25bffemch6DJHdq1yXPx", "messageID": "msg_cfa9e2dba001u083KfeG6aUreJ", "type": "text", "text": "\"An intelligent production line of an automotive parts manufacturing enterprise adopts a Siemens S7-1500 PLC as the main controller, and connects 28 distributed I/O modules (ET 200SP), 12 servo drives (Sinamics V90 PN), 8 barcode scanners (with Profinet interface), and 4 industrial robots (KUKA KR C4, Profinet device) via the Profinet IO protocol. The following problems occur during line operation, and there is no third-party O&M team support, so the on-site engineer must resolve them independently:\nThe production line intermittently generates a “Profinet IO communication timeout” alarm (approximately 3–5 times per day). When the alarm is triggered, some IO devices (random) go offline. After the PLC is restarted, communication is temporarily restored, but the failure reoccurs frequently;\n